to_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt` / `_decrypt` | API shape: `(c, clen_p, m, mlen, ad, adlen, nsec, npub, k)` / `(m, mlen_p, nsec, c, clen, ad, adlen, npub, k)`; exercise with `mlen ∈ {0, 16, 17, 100}`, `adlen ∈ {0, 16, 100}`, `clen_p`/`mlen_p` NULL and non-NULL, `nsec = NULL`. All must return `-1` with `errno = ENOSYS` and leave every out-param untouched | aead_aes256gcm.c:68-97 |\n| `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_detached` / `_decrypt_detached` | API shape with separate `mac`/`maclen_p`; exercise `maclen_p` NULL and non-NULL, `m = NULL` on decrypt. Must return `-1`, `errno = ENOSYS`, `*maclen_p` untouched | aead_aes256gcm.c:57-66, :78-87 |\n| `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_beforenm` | precomputation shape: caller allocates a `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_state` (or `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_statebytes()` = 512 bytes, 16-byte aligned) and calls with a 32-byte `k`. Must return `-1`, `errno = ENOSYS`, and leave `*st_` untouched/uninitialized | aead_aes256gcm.c:99-104 |\n| `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_afternm` / `_decrypt_afternm` / `_encrypt_detached_afternm` / `_decrypt_detached_afternm` | same shapes as the non-`afternm` calls but with a trailing `const crypto_aead_aes256gcm_state *st_` in place of `k`; call each with a zero-filled 512-byte state (since `beforenm` cannot succeed), `mlen ∈ {0, 16, 100}`, `adlen ∈ {0, 16}`, out-pointers NULL and non-NULL. All must return `-1` with `errno = ENOSYS` | aead_aes256gcm.c:106-149 |\n| aes256gcm variant selection | `crypto_aead/aes256gcm/aesni/aead_aes256gcm_aesni.c` and `armcrypto/aead_aes256gcm_armcrypto.c` are compiled but their whole bodies are inside `#ifdef HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H`/`HAVE_ARMCRYPTO` guards, so they contribute NO symbols; the stub block in `aead_aes256gcm.c` provides all 9 operational entry points | aead_aes256gcm.c:50-51,157 |\n| `sodium_misuse` behaviour (affects every `mlen > MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` config) | `_misuse_handler` is a `static` file-scope pointer, default `NULL`; unless the test calls `sodium_set_misuse_handler()`, `sodium_