{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_drcpyxblacicro6urxsfjqfv2x27bpo2eg775gnrg2srq45r7hlq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both deliverables are written and validated (pure table-body rows, no headers/prose, correct column counts).\n\n## Files\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/.phaseA/errors_G3.md` — **80 lines / 80 rows** (4 columns each)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/.phaseA/configs_G3.md` — **137 lines / 137 rows** (3 columns each)\n\n## Key findings (all verified from source, not assumed)\n\n**aes256gcm unavailable path — VERIFIED.** It is *not* `sodium_misuse()`. `crypto_aead/aes256gcm/aead_aes256gcm.c:50-51` opens `#if !((HAVE_ARMCRYPTO && NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN) || (HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H && HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H))`, and each of the 9 operational entry points is exactly `errno = ENOSYS; return -1;` (ENOSYS = 38 on Linux; the file even falls back `#define ENOSYS ENXIO` if undefined). `is_available()` returns `0`.\n\nCritically, **7 aes256gcm symbols are OUTSIDE that `#if` and work normally**: `keybytes`(32), `nsecbytes`(0), `npubbytes`(12), `abytes`(16), `messagebytes_max`(68719476704), `statebytes`() = `(512+15)&~15` = **512**, and `keygen` (which really does fill 32 random bytes despite `is_available() == 0`). Also `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_decrypt`/`_decrypt_afternm` do **not** set `*mlen_p = 0` on failure — unlike every aegis/chacha combined decrypt.\n\n**No runtime `assert()` exists anywhere in `crypto_aead/`.** Every assertion is `COMPILER_ASSERT(X)` = `(void) sizeof(char[(X)?1:-1])` (`private/common.h:25`), which is compile-time only. So no `assert`-sourced SIGABRT is reachable in G3, `NDEBUG` notwithstanding.\n\n**No `#if SIZE_MAX > 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFULL`-style guards** in 1.0.23 `crypto_aead/`; all limits go through `crypto_aead_*_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` macros over `SODIUM_SIZE_MAX = SODIUM_MIN(UINT64_MAX, SIZE_MAX)`.\n\n**No `nsec != NULL` rejection anywhere** — `nsec` is `(void) nsec` discarded in all 5 primitives; `NSECBYTES == 0` throughout.\n\n**Notable asymmetries captured as rows:**\n- aegis `_encrypt_detached` on oversize → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT, but `_decrypt_detached` on oversize → plain `return -1`.\n- aegis `_encrypt_detached` writes `*maclen_p = 32` *before* the length check, so the store is observable prior to the abort.\n- The five `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` values are all different: aegis128l/aegis256 `2305843009213693951` (2^61−1), chacha20poly1305 `18446744073709551599` (2^64−17), chacha20poly1305_**ietf** `274877906880` (64·(2^32−1)), xchacha20poly1305_ietf `18446744073709551599`, aes256gcm `68719476704`.\n- `_encrypt_detached` bypasses the combined function's `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` abort. For chacha20poly1305_ietf this is still caught downstream by `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor_ic`'s counter guard (`stream_chacha20.c:145-148`) → SIGABRT; for the non-IETF and xchacha variants **no rejection is possible at all** (their stream guard is `> SODIUM_SIZE_MAX`, unfireable for a `u64` argument).\n- Tag-failure zeroing is conditional on `m != NULL` in all five: `memset(m, 0, mlen)` then `-1`; with `m == NULL` the raw `crypto_verify_*` result is returned and nothing is written (verify-only mode is a supported configuration, since `m` is deliberately absent from every header's `nonnull` list).\n- aegis uses `crypto_verify_32` (ABYTES 32); the three poly1305 variants use `crypto_verify_16` (ABYTES 16).\n- `_decrypt_detached` has no `clen >= ABYTES` gate, so `clen = 0`/`clen = 5` are legal there while rejected by the combined `_decrypt`.\n- Dead-but-present branches recorded: `aegis128l_mac`/`aegis256_mac` `maclen ∉ {16,32}` → `memset(mac,0,maclen); return -1`, and the `maclen == 16` tag variants — unreachable because `maclen` is hard-coded to ABYTES=32 by the AEAD wrappers.\n\n**Block/partial-block shapes** in configs were derived from the actual rates: aegis128l `RATE 32` with a 64-byte `absorb2` fast loop (so adlen 0/1..31/32/33/64/100 are all distinct), aegis256 `RATE 16` with a 32-byte `absorb2` loop, and the poly1305 variants' 64-byte chacha blocks + 16-byte poly blocks + the `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072` chunk restart (mlen 131072/131073/262144 are distinct paths; encrypt chunks while decrypt does one un-chunked pass). The xchacha `chunk = mlen <= 64*(0xffffffff-1) ? 131072 : mlen` single-pass branch is recorded as record-only (needs ~256 GiB)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":115061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":350,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01H2nXwNYPpnmRZkHiYVLhNM","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"aba06e28-ec8b-418c-9f94-7a1b97b74189","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:17:23.151Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase A tables: crypto_aead"}
