N2_INCORRECT_TYPE`, base64 failures, post-decode `validate_inputs` codes, trailing characters), plus all `argon2_encode_string` `ENCODING_FAIL` sites.\n- `blake2b-long.c` — `outlen > UINT32_MAX` and `outlen == 0` (only two real failures; the `TRY` sites otherwise cannot fail because `blake2b_update` always returns 0).\n- scrypt — `pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256.c`, `crypto_scrypt-common.c` (`escrypt_parse_setting`/`escrypt_r`/`escrypt_gensalt_r`/`encode64*`/`decode64*`), `nosse` (`N` not a power of 2, `N < 2`, `N > UINT32_MAX`, `r*p >= 2^30`, `r==0`, `p==0`, three overflow/`ENOMEM` guards), `scrypt_platform.c`, and the `escrypt_PBKDF2_SHA256` **SIGABRT** at `dkLen > 0x1fffffffe0`.\n\n**`$ROOT/.phaseA/configs_G2.md` — 148 lines (148 config rows)**\n\nCovers `crypto_pwhash` × {ARGON2I13, ARGON2ID13} × opslimit/memlimit/outlen/passwdlen grids; the `blake2b_long` outlen shape boundaries (64/65/96/97/1000); the low-level `argon2_ctx`/`argon2_hash`/`argon2*_hash_raw`/`_hash_encoded`/`argon2_verify`/`argon2_decode_string`/`argon2_encode_string`/`argon2_validate_inputs` with `lanes`/`threads`/`m_cost`/`t_cost` combinations; all six `argon2_fill_segment_ref` / `index_alpha` code paths; scrypt `pickparams` branch-A vs branch-B with worked-out `(N, r, p)` triples; `_ll` with the requested `N`/`r`/`p` grid; and every constant accessor in all four public headers with its exact x86-64 value.\n\n## Notable findings worth flagging to the caller\n\n1. **No `assert()` anywhere in `crypto_pwhash/`.** Despite `NDEBUG` being absent, the only abort paths in this subtree are two `sodium_misuse()` calls: `crypto_pwhash.c:169` (bad `alg` in `crypto_pwhash_str_alg`) and `pbkdf2-sha256.c:64` (`dkLen > 0x1fffffffe0`, reachable only by calling the internal symbol directly — `escrypt_kdf_nosse` rejects such `buflen` with `EFBIG` first, and the two bounds are exactly equal).\n2. **`crypto_pwhash_str_alg` aborts rather than returning `-1`** for an out-of-range `alg`, unlike `crypto_pwhash` which returns `-1`. This asymmetry is the single most likely divergence point for a Rust port.\n3. **libsodium 1.0.23 has no `str[crypto_pwhash_STRBYTES-1] != 0` guard** in the argon2 `_str_verify` functions. `argon2_verify` calls `strlen(encoded)` unbounded, so a non-NUL-terminated `str` is UB. Only the scrypt path bounds-checks (`sodium_strnlen(str, 102) != 101`).\n4. **`crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256` enforces neither `OPSLIMIT_MIN/MAX` nor `MEMLIMIT_MIN/MAX`.** `opslimit = 0` is silently clamped up to 32768 by `pickparams`, and `memlimit` above `MEMLIMIT_MAX` is accepted. `pickparams` unconditionally returns 0, so all four `pickparams(...) != 0` guards in that file are dead code.\n5. Two `argon2` branches are provably dead: the `memory_blocks < 2*SYNC_POINTS*lanes` clamp in `argon2_ctx` (pre-empted by `validate_inputs`' `m_cost < 8*lanes` check) and every `x > UINT32_MAX` test applied to a `uint32_t` field.\n6. Derived invariant for scrypt: in `pickparams` branch B, `p >= 1` always holds (`maxrp >= 256*opslimit/memlimit >= 8`), so `escrypt_kdf_nosse`'s `p == 0` rejection is unreachable from the high-level scrypt API — only from `_ll`.\n7. `memlimit = 0` is a legal, *fast* input to `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256`, yielding `(N=2, r=8, p=512)` — useful as a cheap differential test vector.","usage":{"total_tokens":179518,"tool_uses":41,"duration_ms":797236},"uuid":"4c293adc-6705-4f82-8bae-647463728ddd","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zsk6djwvtddygibrz5lnmcrofbnoaqd4ju6tyhs2qic673rvpf3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both deliverables are written and well-formed (every line is a table body row with the exact column count; no headers or prose).\n\n**Line counts: `errors_G1.md` = 159 rows, `configs_G1.md` = 174 rows.**\n\n## Key build-configuration findings (these drive most of the semantics)\n\nConfirmed by compiling a probe on this host plus reading `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` (no `HAVE_*`, no `NDEBUG`, `-std=c99`, x86-64 Linux):\n\n- **`HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC` is NOT defined** (no `MAP_ANON`/`HAVE_MMAP`/`HAVE_POSIX_MEMALIGN`/`WINAPI_DESKTOP`). So `sodium_malloc` is just `malloc(size ? size : 1)`, `sodium_free` is plain `free`, and **all canary/guard-page/`_out_of_bounds()` machinery is dead code**. There is no `SIZE_MAX - page_size*4` pre-check in `sodium_malloc`.\n- **`sodium_mlock`/`munlock`/`mprotect_noaccess`/`readonly`/`readwrite` ALWAYS return `-1` with `errno=ENOSYS`.** `sodium_munlock` zeroes the buffer *before* failing.\n- **`sodium_stackzero(len)` compiles to an empty body** — a no-op for every `len`.\n- **`sodium_crit_enter`/`leave` are the no-op stubs returning 0**, so every `return -1` in `sodium_init` / `sodium_set_misuse_handler` is unreachable; `sodium_init` returns 0 then 1 forever.\n- **`_cpuid()` is the zero-filling stub**, so `_sodium_runtime_get_cpu_features()` always returns `-1` and **all 12 `sodium_runtime_has_*()` return 0**.\n- **`HAVE_AMD64_ASM` off** → the `nlen==8/12/24/64` fast paths in `sodium_increment`/`add`/`sub` are dead; one generic loop for all lengths.\n- **`HAVE_LINUX_COMPATIBLE_GETRANDOM` IS live** in both randombytes files (via `__linux__` + `SYS_getrandom`, which are platform macros not `HAVE_*`), so the default RNG uses `syscall(SYS_getrandom)` chunked at 256 bytes, not `/dev/urandom`. `BLOCK_ON_DEV_RANDOM` is also live. `HAVE_GETPID` is undefined → **no fork detection**. `TLS` expands to nothing (`__STDC_VERSION__ == 199901L`) → the \"thread-local\" internal RNG state is a plain global.\n- `SIZE_MAX > 0x4000000000ULL` is live → `randombytes_buf_deterministic(size > 256 GiB)` → SIGABRT. `assert(buf_len <= SIZE_MAX)` in `randombytes()` can never fire.\n\n## Non-obvious semantics worth flagging to whoever writes the tests\n\n1. **`sodium_hex2bin` and `sodium_base642bin` return `-1` but still report a non-zero `*bin_len`** when the *only* failure is the `hex_end==NULL`/`b64_end==NULL` \"trailing garbage\" check — `bin_pos = 0` happens at codecs.c:90/:327, *before* the out-param check at :94/:335.\n2. **errno gets overwritten**: an `ERANGE` (buffer-full) failure ends up reporting `EINVAL` whenever `hex_end`/`b64_end` is NULL. The `acc_len > 4` / non-canonical-trailing-bits rejection in `sodium_base642bin` (codecs.c:319) sets **no errno at all**.\n3. **`sodium_bin2base64` zero-fills the entire remaining output buffer up to `b64_maxlen`** (codecs.c:243-245); `sodium_bin2hex` writes only `bin_len*2+1` bytes. Easy Rust-port divergence.\n4. **Putting `'='` in `ignore` breaks padded base64 decoding** (`\"AA==\"`, variant 1 → `-1`/`ERANGE`): the main loop eats the pads as ignorable chars, then `skip_padding` runs off the end.\n5. **`strchr(ignore, c)` matches the NUL terminator**, so with any non-NULL `ignore` (even `\"\"`) embedded NUL bytes are silently skipped in both `sodium_hex2bin` and `sodium_base642bin`.\n6. **`sodium_unpad` writes `*unpadded_buflen_p` unconditionally at utils.c:810, even when it returns `-1`** for invalid padding, and it never NULL-checks that pointer (NULL → SIGSEGV). Contrast `sodium_pad`, which *does* NULL-check `padded_buflen_p`.\n7. `sodium_base64_encoded_len` aborts (misuse) on the overflow condition, so the `(size_t)SIZE_MAX` result of the public `sodium_base64_ENCODED_LEN` macro is unreachable through the function.\n8. `sodium_ip2bin` validates an IPv6 zone/scope id and then **discards** it; `sodium_allocarray` uses `>=` (so `allocarray(1, SIZE_MAX)` and `allocarray(SIZE_MAX, 1)` both fail with `ENOMEM`); `GARBAGE_VALUE` is `0xdb` although `utils.h` documents `0xd0`.\n9. Directly reachable abort: `randombytes_sysrandom_implementation.buf(p, 0)` (the struct is an exported symbol) hits `assert(chunk_size > 0)` → SIGABRT, bypassing `randombytes_buf`'s `size > 0` guard.\n10. `randombytes_set_implementation(NULL)` returns 0 and silently reverts to the default impl on the next call; `randombytes_close()` returns `-1` if you install either built-in impl and close before any stir."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":150233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":256,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VeFjfnRmdqN6GMu9bf1WKC","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"02658eb7-b7ae-4f73-bb88-c770b76dc430","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:20:57.711Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase A tables: sodium+randombytes"}
