he ristretto255 generator `e2 f2 ae 0a 6a bc 4e 71 a8 84 a9 61 c5 00 51 5f 58 e3 0b 6a a5 82 dd 8d b6 a6 59 45 e0 8d 2d 76` x scalar shapes {1, 2, L-1, random}. Only `t[31] &= 127` is applied - NEVER clamped, so `n = 1` returns `p` verbatim | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:21-26 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255` | `p` = a random valid element (`crypto_core_ristretto255_random()`) x random `n` | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:18-26 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255` | `n` = all-0xff -> `t` = `ff ff ... ff 7f` = 2^255-1; valid | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:24 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255` | `n` = L+1 must equal `n` = 1; `n` = L+2 must equal `n` = 2 (ristretto encodes the quotient group, so scalars are mod L) | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:21-26 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255_base` | scalar shapes {1, 2, L-1, all-0xff, random}, unclamped. `n = 1` must return the generator encoding `e2f2ae0a...2d76`. `t = q` aliases the output buffer | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:34-51 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255_base` vs `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255` | consistency: `base(n)` must equal `mult(n, generator)`, via `ge25519_scalarmult_base` vs `ge25519_scalarmult` | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:25 vs :45 |\n| `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255_bytes` / `_ristretto255_scalarbytes` | 32, 32 | crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c:53-63 |\n| `crypto_core_ed25519_add` | two random valid main-subgroup points; also (B, B) -> 2B, (B, identity `01 00..00`) -> B, (P, -P) -> identity. `ge25519_p3_add` is the extended-coordinate complete addition | crypto_core/ed25519/core_ed25519.c:29-42 (ed25519_ref10.c:1030-1041) |\n| `crypto_core_ed25519_add` | non-canonical but on-curve `p` (e.g. `ed ff ff ... ff 7f` =