{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wes6lgg2thbqcfw46onkocrcqlcbtk5eapkobnhaizorev6g7lda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both deliverables are written. `c_src/` and `src/` untouched.\n\n## Line counts\n- `$ROOT/.phaseA/errors_G4.md` — **135 lines** (135 table body rows, all validated as well-formed 4-column rows)\n- `$ROOT/.phaseA/configs_G4.md` — **149 lines** (149 table body rows, all validated as well-formed 3-column rows)\n\n## Build-config facts verified (not assumed)\n`c_src/build/CMakeFiles/sodium.dir/flags.make` contains only `C_DEFINES = -Dsodium_EXPORTS` and `C_FLAGS = -fPIC -std=gnu99`. Therefore:\n- **`assert()` is ACTIVE** (no `-DNDEBUG`) — confirmed live by triggering `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final(state, out, 256)` → glibc assertion message + exit 134.\n- **poly1305 uses `poly1305_donna32.h`** (`HAVE_TI_MODE` is nowhere defined; only appears in `#ifdef`). The SSE2 impl is unreachable — its selector is gated on `HAVE_TI_MODE && HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H`.\n- **blake2b uses `blake2b_compress_ref`**; `crypto_verify_n` uses the portable `volatile uint16_t` byte loop (`HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H` and `HAVE_INLINE_ASM` both undefined); keccak1600 uses `keccak1600_ref_*`.\n\n## Findings that contradict the task brief (corrected in the tables)\n1. **There is NO turboshake domain-byte range check.** `crypto_xof_turboshake{128,256}_init_with_domain` accepts all 256 byte values and returns `0` — verified for 0x00, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x80, 0xff. The `DOMAIN_STANDARD` for all four XOFs is `0x1F`.\n2. **`crypto_xof_*` has no `_final`, `_absorb`, or `_clone`.** Exported set per primitive: `<p>`, `_init`, `_init_with_domain`, `_update`, `_squeeze`, `_statebytes`, `_blockbytes`, `_domain_standard`. Absorb is `_update`; finalisation is implicit in the first `_squeeze`.\n3. **`crypto_core_keccak1600` has no `_absorb`, no `_pad`, and no rate/capacity parameter** — hence no rate validity check anywhere. Exports are `_init`, `_xor_bytes`, `_extract_bytes`, `_permute_12`, `_permute_24`, `_statebytes` (224). Zero bounds checking: `offset + length > 200` is silent OOB.\n4. **SHA-3 exports only `sha3256` (rate 136) and `sha3512` (rate 72)** — no 224/384. Domain byte `0x06`.\n5. **`crypto_generichash_BYTES_MIN`/`KEYBYTES_MIN` (16) are NOT enforced** — `outlen = 1` and `keylen = 1` both return `0`. Only `1 <= outlen <= 64` and `keylen <= 64` are checked.\n6. **`_final` never validates `outlen` against the `outlen` given at `_init`** — `_init(...,32)` then `_final(...,64)` returns `0`.\n7. **Three distinct abort/reject sites for the same nominal condition in `_final`:** `outlen == 0` → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT, `outlen` 65..255 → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT, `outlen >= 256` → failed `assert`/SIGABRT — while `_init` and the one-shot return `-1` for the same values.\n8. **Key-NULL asymmetry:** `crypto_generichash(out,32,in,1,NULL,5)` → SIGABRT, but `crypto_generichash_init(state,NULL,5,32)` → `0` (silently unkeyed).\n9. **hkdf's only abort path:** `_extract`/`_extract_init` with `salt == NULL && salt_len > 0` → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT via `crypto_auth_hmacsha*_init`.\n10. `crypto_kdf_hkdf_sha256_BYTES_MAX = 8160` (0xff·32), `sha512 = 16320` (0xff·64), both `BYTES_MIN = 0`; `statebytes` 208/416. All confirmed at runtime."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":891,"cache_read_input_tokens":220630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":891,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Qmz3yyeiwdcT9MBKBzhXKC","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"11f0d086-b5b4-4172-af0d-2e31d9f36208","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:23:07.081Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase A tables: hash/mac/xof/kdf"}
