26e8958f…fc85`, `c7176a70…03fa`\n- valid but off the main subgroup (only `_pk_to_curve25519`'s 3rd branch): `03/04/05/06/09/0a 00…00`, `ff`×32\n- non-canonical S: `S = L`, `L+1`, `ff`×32 (and `L-1` **is** canonical)\n\n**Notable semantic asymmetries recorded in column 3:**\n- `crypto_sign_ed25519_open` zeroes `m` on *signature* failure but **not** on the `smlen < 64` path; `*mlen_p = 0` on both.\n- All `*_open_detached` MAC failures leave `m` completely untouched (no memset, no length pointer).\n- `crypto_secretstream…_pull` writes `*mlen_p = 0` and `*tag_p = 0xff` **before** any validation, so those are observable on every failure path; state is not advanced on MAC failure.\n- `crypto_box_seal` still `memcpy`s the ephemeral pk into `c[0..31]` even when the inner `crypto_box_easy` fails.\n- `crypto_auth_hmacsha{256,512}_init` with `key == NULL` and `keylen > blocksize` bypasses the `sodium_misuse` guard entirely → NULL deref/SIGSEGV, not a clean abort.\n- `crypto_secretstream` has **no** end-of-stream flag: pushing after `TAG_FINAL` succeeds (returns 0) because `TAG_FINAL & TAG_REKEY != 0` already rekeyed the state; and `_pull` does **not** validate the decrypted tag byte.\n- The secretstream message-padding formula `(0x10 - sizeof block + mlen) & 0xf` reduces to `mlen & 0xf` (the in-source comment flags it as a bug) — the port must reproduce it exactly.\n- `crypto_secretbox_detached` chunks the encrypt path at `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072`, while `_open_detached` does not; the xchacha20 variant chunks in neither direction.\n- API-surface asymmetry confirmed against `nm -D`: `curve25519xchacha20poly1305` has **no** NaCl combined/afternm API and no `ZEROBYTES`/`BOXZEROBYTES`; `curve25519xsalsa20poly1305` has the NaCl layer under its explicit name but its easy/detached/seal layers exist only under generic `crypto_box_*` names."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":667,"cache_read_input