{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AibE57fEeKSo7GHJksBfui","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t#ifndef softaes_H\n     2\t#    define softaes_H 1\n     3\t\n     4\t#    include <stdint.h>\n     5\t\n     6\t#    include \"private/common.h\"\n     7\t\n     8\ttypedef struct SoftAesBlock {\n     9\t    uint32_t w0;\n    10\t    uint32_t w1;\n    11\t    uint32_t w2;\n    12\t    uint32_t w3;\n    13\t} SoftAesBlock;\n    14\t\n    15\tvoid         softaes_expand_key128(SoftAesBlock rkeys[11], const uint8_t key[16]);\n    16\tvoid         softaes_expand_key256(SoftAesBlock rkeys[15], const uint8_t key[32]);\n    17\tSoftAesBlock softaes_inv_mix_columns(const SoftAesBlock block);\n    18\tvoid         softaes_invert_key_schedule128(SoftAesBlock rkeys[11]);\n    19\tvoid         softaes_invert_key_schedule256(SoftAesBlock rkeys[15]);\n    20\tSoftAesBlock softaes_block_encrypt(const SoftAesBlock block, const SoftAesBlock rk);\n    21\tSoftAesBlock softaes_block_decrypt(const SoftAesBlock block, const SoftAesBlock rk);\n    22\tSoftAesBlock softaes_block_encryptlast(const SoftAesBlock block, const SoftAesBlock rk);\n    23\tSoftAesBlock softaes_block_decryptlast(const SoftAesBlock block, const SoftAesBlock rk);\n    24\t\n    25\tstatic inline SoftAesBlock\n    26\tsoftaes_block_load(const uint8_t in[16])\n    27\t{\n    28\t    const SoftAesBlock out = { LOAD32_LE(in + 0), LOAD32_LE(in + 4), LOAD32_LE(in + 8),\n    29\t                               LOAD32_LE(in + 12) };\n    30\t    return out;\n    31\t}\n    32\t\n    33\tstatic inline SoftAesBlock\n    34\tsoftaes_block_load64x2(const uint64_t a, const uint64_t b)\n    35\t{\n    36\t    const SoftAesBlock out = { (uint32_t) b, (uint32_t) (b >> 32), (uint32_t) a,\n    37\t                               (uint32_t) (a >> 32) };\n    38\t    return out;\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\tstatic inline void\n    42\tsoftaes_block_store(uint8_t out[16], const SoftAesBlock in)\n    43\t{\n    44\t    STORE32_LE(out + 0, in.w0);\n    45\t    STORE32_LE(out + 4, in.w1);\n    46\t    STORE32_LE(out + 8, in.w2);\n    47\t    STORE32_LE(out + 12, in.w3);\n    48\t}\n    49\t\n    50\tstatic inline SoftAesBlock\n    51\tsoftaes_block_xor(const SoftAesBlock a, const SoftAesBlock b)\n    52\t{\n    53\t    const SoftAesBlock out = { a.w0 ^ b.w0, a.w1 ^ b.w1, a.w2 ^ b.w2, a.w3 ^ b.w3 };\n    54\t    return out;\n    55\t}\n    56\t\n    57\tstatic inline SoftAesBlock\n    58\tsoftaes_block_and(const SoftAesBlock a, const SoftAesBlock b)\n    59\t{\n    60\t    const SoftAesBlock out = { a.w0 & b.w0, a.w1 & b.w1, a.w2 & b.w2, a.w3 & b.w3 };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JQEcLjQFThN8j4oYTXU8DB","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"f086ad69-8b75-436c-8660-1784f53ef5f0","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:25:34.049Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase A tables: core/scalarmult/stream/kem"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ue2cqka2sbrxrw5pezgaxx3mc4uxdnvkhctmn6if4vvwfjkpfu5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01FRwnaLrRx5yLxcrZ1zFyQ7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, os\nGROUPS = [\n (\"G1\", \"`sodium/` + `randombytes/` — `sodium_*` utils, codecs, core, runtime, version, RNG\"),\n (\"G2\", \"`crypto_pwhash/` — argon2i / argon2id / scrypt\"),\n (\"G3\", \"`crypto_aead/` — aegis128l, aegis256, aes256gcm, chacha20poly1305, xchacha20poly1305\"),\n (\"G4\", \"hashes / MACs / XOFs / KDFs — blake2b, sha2, sha3, shake, turboshake, keccak1600, poly1305, siphash, verify, hkdf, kdf_blake2b\"),\n (\"G5\", \"`crypto_box` / `crypto_secretbox` / `crypto_secretstream` / `crypto_kx` / `crypto_sign` / `crypto_auth`\"),\n (\"G6\", \"`crypto_core` / `crypto_scalarmult` / `crypto_stream` / `crypto_kem` / `crypto_ipcrypt`\"),\n]\ndef cells(line):\n    parts = re.split(r'(?<!\\\\)\\|', line.rstrip('\\n'))\n    if parts and parts[0].strip()=='': parts=parts[1:]\n    if parts and parts[-1].strip()=='': parts=parts[:-1]\n    return [p.strip() for p in parts]\n\ndef build(kind, out, title, intro, header, rowfmt):\n    L = [title, \"\", intro, \"\"]\n    total = 0\n    counts = {}\n    for g, desc in GROUPS:\n        rows = [cells(l) for l in open(f\".phaseA/{kind}_{g}.md\") if l.strip()]\n        counts[g] = len(rows)\n        total += len(rows)\n    L.append(\"## Row counts\\n\")\n    L.append(\"| group | scope | rows |\")\n    L.append(\"|---|---|---|\")\n    for g, desc in GROUPS:\n        L.append(f\"| **{g}** | {desc} | {counts[g]} |\")\n    L.append(f\"| | **TOTAL** | **{total}** |\")\n    L.append(\"\")\n    for g, desc in GROUPS:\n        rows = [cells(l) for l in open(f\".phaseA/{kind}_{g}.md\") if l.strip()]\n        L.append(f\"## {g} — {desc}\\n\")\n        L.append(header)\n        L.append(\"|\" + \"---|\"*header.count(\"|\") if False else None)\n        L.pop()\n        L.append(\"|\" + \"---|\"*(header.count(\"|\")-1))\n        for i, c in enumerate(rows, 1):\n            L.append(rowfmt(f\"{g}-{i:03d}\", c))\n        L.append(\"\")\n    open(out,\"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(x for x in L if x is not None) + \"\\n\")\n    return total, counts\n\net, ec = build(\n    \"errors\", \"ERRORS.md\",\n    \"# ERRORS.md — the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A / gate for Phase C)\",\n    \"Mechanically derived from the C source in `c_src/libsodium`: **every** distinct\\n\"\n    \"way the library rejects or errors on input — every `return -1` / `return NULL` /\\n\"\n    \"error-enum return, every `sodium_misuse()` (which runs the installed handler and\\n\"\n    \"then `abort()`s → SIGABRT), every active `assert()`, every explicit range / bounds\\n\"\n    \"/ overflow check, every NULL check the code itself performs, every `errno = ...`\\n\"\n    \"assignment, and every out-of-range enum / `alg` / variant value.\\n\\n\"\n    \"Build configuration these rows describe (see `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`): **no `HAVE_*`\\n\"\n    \"macros** and **no `NDEBUG`** — so every `#ifdef HAVE_*` selects the portable\\n\"\n    \"fallback and `assert()` is live. Target: x86-64 Linux, `SIZE_MAX == 2^64-1`.\\n\\n\"\n    \"Column 4 is the `file:line` the row was derived from. The `test` column names the\\n\"\n    \"differential test that constructs the condition and asserts C and Rust reject it\\n\"\n    \"identically (same error code / sentinel / signal / side effects), or states why the\\n\"\n    \"row is not constructible.\",\n    \"| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | source | test |\",\n    lambda idx, c: f\"| {idx} | {c[0]} | {c[1]} | {c[2]} | {c[3]} | |\",\n)\nct, cc = build(\n    \"configs\", \"CONFIGS.md\",\n    \"# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A / gate for Phase B)\",\n    \"Mechanically derived from the C source: every meaningful **combination** of\\n\"\n    \"(runtime option / mode / flag) × (input shape) that the C code actually treats\\n\"\n    \"differently for *valid* input. Rows come from the `if` / `switch` / `#ifdef`\\n\"\n    \"branches the C takes, the block / rate / chunk boundaries its loops distinguish,\\n\"\n    \"and the FULL set of public entry points — including the lowest-level ones, not\\n\"\n    \"just the one-shot convenience wrappers.\\n\\n\"\n    \"Build configuration: **no `HAVE_*` macros**, **no `NDEBUG`** (portable/ref/soft\\n\"\n    \"implementations, live `assert()`). Target x86-64 Linux.\\n\\n\"\n    \"Each row is exercised with **many randomised inputs** (fixed seed) by the named\\n\"\n    \"test, comparing the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` byte-for-byte through `dlsym`.\",\n    \"| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | source | test | [ ] |\",\n    lambda idx, c: f\"| {idx} | {c[0]} | {c[1]} | {c[2]} | | [ ] |\",\n)\nprint(\"ERRORS.md rows:\", et, ec)\nprint(\"CONFIGS.md rows:\", ct, cc)\nPY\nwc -l ERRORS.md CONFIGS.md","description":"Assemble ERRORS.md and CONFIGS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":260031,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":955,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"7ec4940f-8772-4817-9b46-bd09fcdefa57","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:25:37.735Z"}
