he clamped forms** — clamping forces `t ∈ [2^254, 2^255)` and `t ≡ 0 mod 8`, so a multiple of `8L > 2^255` would be required. It IS reachable in the `_noclamp` forms (`n = L…7L`, or `n = 00…00 80`).\n- **`crypto_core_ed25519_add`/`_sub` do NOT validate canonicality, small order, or subgroup membership** — only `frombytes`. Non-canonical and small-order points are accepted, unlike `_is_valid_point`.\n- **`crypto_scalarmult_curve25519`'s all-zero-output check is dead code** in this build: every 255-bit-masked small-order x is already in the 7-entry blocklist.\n- **8 of the 9 `sodium_misuse()` sites in `stream_chacha20.c` are unreachable on x86-64** (`SODIUM_SIZE_MAX == 2^64-1` and `mlen` is `unsigned long long`). The only practically reachable one is `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor_ic`'s counter check: `ic + ceil(mlen/64) > 2^32` (smallest case `mlen=65, ic=0xffffffff`). `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_ext_xor_ic` has **no** such guard and silently corrupts the nonce on wrap.\n- **No `crypto_ipcrypt_*_encrypt_ip_str` / `_decrypt_ip_str` exists in 1.0.23.** Every `crypto_ipcrypt_*` entry point is `void` with zero rejection branches; there is also a `pfx` variant (not in the task brief) with an IPv4-mapped-vs-IPv6 path split and a degenerate-key branch (`k[0..15] == k[16..31]` → re-expand from `k ⊕ 0x5a`), shared with `ndx`.\n- **Absent API surface** (confirmed against `nm -D`): no `crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform`, no `crypto_core_ed25519_from_string_ro`, and no `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_string_ro`/`_nu` — only `_from_string` and (ed25519 only) `_from_string_nu`.\n- **`hash_alg` out of range** → `errno = EINVAL; return -1` (core_h2c.c:129-131). The two active `assert(h_len <= 0xff)` are unreachable from the public API (h_len is only ever 48/64/96). `ctx_len > 0xff` is not an error but a distinct DST-derivation path."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1720,"cache_read_input_tokens":2