{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NkuAQFzzbAZgNBK8UExRKE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — the CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A / gate for Phase B)\n2\t\n3\tMechanically derived from the C source: every meaningful **combination** of\n4\t(runtime option / mode / flag) × (input shape) that the C code actually treats\n5\tdifferently for *valid* input. Rows come from the `if` / `switch` / `#ifdef`\n6\tbranches the C takes, the block / rate / chunk boundaries its loops distinguish,\n7\tand the FULL set of public entry points — including the lowest-level ones, not\n8\tjust the one-shot convenience wrappers.\n9\t\n10\tBuild configuration: **no `HAVE_*` macros**, **no `NDEBUG`** (portable/ref/soft\n11\timplementations, live `assert()`). Target x86-64 Linux.\n12\t\n13\tEach row is exercised with **many randomised inputs** (fixed seed) by the named\n14\ttest, comparing the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` byte-for-byte through `dlsym`.\n15\t\n16\t## Row counts\n17\t\n18\t| group | scope | rows |\n19\t|---|---|---|\n20\t| **G1** | `sodium/` + `randombytes/` — `sodium_*` utils, codecs, core, runtime, version, RNG | 174 |\n21\t| **G2** | `crypto_pwhash/` — argon2i / argon2id / scrypt | 148 |\n22\t| **G3** | `crypto_aead/` — aegis128l, aegis256, aes256gcm, chacha20poly1305, xchacha20poly1305 | 137 |\n23\t| **G4** | hashes / MACs / XOFs / KDFs — blake2b, sha2, sha3, shake, turboshake, keccak1600, poly1305, siphash, verify, hkdf, kdf_blake2b | 149 |\n24\t| **G5** | `crypto_box` / `crypto_secretbox` / `crypto_secretstream` / `crypto_kx` / `crypto_sign` / `crypto_auth` | 142 |\n25\t| **G6** | `crypto_core` / `crypto_scalarmult` / `crypto_stream` / `crypto_kem` / `crypto_ipcrypt` | 173 |\n26\t| | **TOTAL** | **923** |\n27\t\n28\t## G1 — `sodium/` + `randombytes/` — `sodium_*` utils, codecs, core, runtime, version, RNG\n29\t\n30\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | source | test | [ ] |\n31\t|--