{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"af45fa1ab0c7a1a9c","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UPVb62KCU2WLXnLML5Z8s2","description":"Phase B+C tests: crypto_pwhash","subagent_type":"general-purpose","is_backgrounded":true,"spawn_depth":1,"task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are writing **differential tests** that verify a Rust translation of **libsodium 1.0.23** matches the C reference byte-for-byte, for ONE module group.\n\nROOT = `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust` (this is the crate root and your cwd)\n\n## Read these FIRST\n1. `$ROOT/.phaseA/HARNESS.md` — the test-harness contract. Follow it exactly.\n2. `$ROOT/tests/common/mod.rs` — the harness implementation.\n3. `$ROOT/tests/t03_hashes.rs` and `$ROOT/tests/t05_aead_errors.rs` — worked examples of a Phase B test and a Phase C test (including the out-of-process `sodium_misuse` pattern). Copy their style.\n4. `$ROOT/CONFIGS.md` section **`## G2`** — 148 valid-input configuration rows (`G2-001` … `G2-148`). Your Phase B work list.\n5. `$ROOT/ERRORS.md` section **`## G2`** — 223 error rows (`G2-001` … `G2-223`). Your Phase C work list.\n\n## YOUR GROUP (G2) = `crypto_pwhash/`\nC source: `c_src/libsodium/crypto_pwhash/**` (argon2 + scryptsalsa208sha256).\nRust source: `src/crypto_pwhash/**`.\n\nPublic entry points (get exact signatures from `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/crypto_pwhash.h`, `crypto_pwhash_argon2i.h`, `crypto_pwhash_argon2id.h`, `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256.h`; cross-check the real export list with\n`nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libsodium.so | awk '{print $3}' | grep pwhash`).\n\n## Deliverables\n* `$ROOT/tests/t12_pwhash.rs` — Phase B, covering every CONFIGS `## G2` row, with MANY randomised inputs per row (`Rng::new(<fixed seed>)`). Doc-comment each `#[test]` with the `G2-NNN` ids it covers.\n* `$ROOT/tests/t13_pwhash_errors.rs` — Phase C, covering EVERY ERRORS `## G2` row: same return value, same `errno`, same output buffer, same `*out` string. Doc-comment each `#[test]` with the `G2-NNN` ids it covers.\n\n## PERFORMANCE — this is the slow group, plan for it\nArgon2 and scrypt are deliberately expensive. Keep the WHOLE file under ~120 s:\n* Use the **cheapest valid parameters** for the bulk of the randomised runs:\n  argon2i `opslimit = 3` (its MIN), argon2id `opslimit = 1` (its MIN), `memlimit = 8192` (MIN).\n  scrypt: `memlimit = 0` is legal and yields `(N=2, r=8, p=512)` — very fast; also use `_ll` with tiny explicit `N`/`r`/`p`.\n* Run the `INTERACTIVE` presets ONCE each, not in a loop. Do **not** run `MODERATE` or `SENSITIVE` (they need hundreds of MiB and seconds each) — instead assert the *constant accessors* agree and add a comment naming the rows you downscaled.\n* If a test still exceeds ~60 s, cut the input grid and note it.\n\n## Critical correctness notes (verified from source — honour them)\n* `crypto_pwhash_argon2i_OPSLIMIT_MIN` is **3**, `crypto_pwhash_argon2id_OPSLIMIT_MIN` is **1**. `BYTES_MIN=16`, `BYTES_MAX=4294967295`, `MEMLIMIT_MIN=8192`, `MEMLIMIT_MAX=4398046510080` (x86-64).\n* `crypto_pwhash(...)` with an out-of-range `alg` returns `-1` with `errno = EINVAL`, but **`crypto_pwhash_str_alg(...)` falls through its `switch` to `sodium_misuse()` → SIGABRT**. This asymmetry is the single most likely divergence — test `alg` = 0, 1, 2, 3, -1, `i32::MAX`, `i32::MIN` on BOTH, and put the aborting one in a child process.\n* `crypto_pwhash_scryptsalsa208sha256` enforces **neither** OPSLIMIT nor MEMLIMIT bounds; `opslimit = 0` is silently clamped to 32768; `memlimit` above MAX is accepted. Its `pickparams` always returns 0, so those guards are dead.\n* `argon2_verify` calls unbounded `strlen`, so `str` must always be NUL-terminated in your tests (a non-terminated `str` is UB, not a rejection — note the row). The scrypt `_str_verify` DOES bound-check (`sodium_strnlen(str, 102) != 101`).\n* The `ARGON2_*` error enum: internal functions return e.g. `ARGON2_SALT_TOO_SHORT` but the public wrappers map everything to `-1`. Assert what the PUBLIC symbol returns; only assert enum values for internal symbols that are actually exported (check `nm`).\n* `crypto_pwhash_str_verify` / `_str_needs_rehash`: cover malformed prefixes, truncated strings, wrong-variant prefixes, bad `$v=`, bad `m=`/`t=`/`p=`, non-minimal decimals, decimals > UINT32_MAX, bad base64, trailing characters, and `version != 19`.\n* `blake2b_long`: `outlen == 0` and `outlen > UINT32_MAX` are the only real failures; outlen boundaries 64/65/96/97 change the code path.\n* Round-trip: `crypto_pwhash_str` → `_str_verify` must succeed; a one-byte mutation of the hash string must fail identically in C and Rust.\n* `crypto_pwhash_str*` output is a NUL-terminated ASCII string in a `crypto_pwhash_STRBYTES` buffer. Compare the FULL buffer with `canary()` fill so trailing-byte handling is checked, and also compare as a C string.\n\n## Method (iterate until green)\n1. Write the Phase B file; `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test t12_pwhash 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n2. Fix failures. **The C is ALWAYS right — never edit anything under `c_src/`.** On divergence read the C and fix `src/crypto_pwhash/**`. Re-run until green.\n3. Same for the Phase C file (`--test t13_pwhash_errors`).\n4. Finally `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features 2>&1 | tail -40` to confirm nothing else broke.\n\n## Rules\n* Only create/modify: `$ROOT/tests/t12_pwhash.rs`, `$ROOT/tests/t13_pwhash_errors.rs`, and files under `$ROOT/src/crypto_pwhash/` (bug fixes only). Do NOT touch `tests/common/mod.rs`, other tests, `Cargo.toml`, or anything in `c_src/`.\n* Use `timeout` on every command.\n\n## Report back\n* Exact paths + line counts of the two files, and the number of `#[test]`s in each.\n* **Every C/Rust divergence found and the exact fix made** (file + what was wrong). Most important part.\n* Which G2 rows you downscaled or could not construct, and why.\n* Final `cargo test` summary lines.","uuid":"d32a0792-9c4f-4cdf-b251-f02bfdeb56d7","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77"}
