{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WAkFy8Z3gt5MNrF8QyNUwC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A / gate for Phase C)\n2\t\n3\tMechanically derived from the C source in `c_src/libsodium`: **every** distinct\n4\tway the library rejects or errors on input — every `return -1` / `return NULL` /\n5\terror-enum return, every `sodium_misuse()` (which runs the installed handler and\n6\tthen `abort()`s → SIGABRT), every active `assert()`, every explicit range / bounds\n7\t/ overflow check, every NULL check the code itself performs, every `errno = ...`\n8\tassignment, and every out-of-range enum / `alg` / variant value.\n9\t\n10\tBuild configuration these rows describe (see `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`): **no `HAVE_*`\n11\tmacros** and **no `NDEBUG`** — so every `#ifdef HAVE_*` selects the portable\n12\tfallback and `assert()` is live. Target: x86-64 Linux, `SIZE_MAX == 2^64-1`.\n13\t\n14\tColumn 4 is the `file:line` the row was derived from. The `test` column names the\n15\tdifferential test that constructs the condition and asserts C and Rust reject it\n16\tidentically (same error code / sentinel / signal / side effects), or states why the\n17\trow is not constructible.\n18\t\n19\t## Row counts\n20\t\n21\t| group | scope | rows |\n22\t|---|---|---|\n23\t| **G1** | `sodium/` + `randombytes/` — `sodium_*` utils, codecs, core, runtime, version, RNG | 159 |\n24\t| **G2** | `crypto_pwhash/` — argon2i / argon2id / scrypt | 223 |\n25\t| **G3** | `crypto_aead/` — aegis128l, aegis256, aes256gcm, chacha20poly1305, xchacha20poly1305 | 80 |\n26\t| **G4** | hashes / MACs / XOFs / KDFs — blake2b, sha2, sha3, shake, turboshake, keccak1600, poly1305, siphash, verify, hkdf, kdf_blake2b | 135 |\n27\t| **G5** | `crypto_box` / `crypto_secretbox` / `crypto_secretstream` / `crypto_kx` / `crypto_sign` / `crypto_auth` | 110 |\n28\t| **G6** | `crypto_core` / `crypto_scalarmult` / `crypto_stream` / `crypto_kem` / `crypto_ipcrypt` | 149 |\n29\t| | **TOTAL** | **856** |\n30\t\n31\t## G1 — `sodium/` + `randombytes/` — `sodium_*` utils, codecs, core, runtime, version, RNG\n32\t\n33\t| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | source | test |\n34\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n35\t| G1-001 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len >= SIZE_MAX / 2`, e.g. `bin_len = 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF`, any `hex`/`hex_maxlen` (bin never dereferenced before the check) | `SIGABRT` (sodium_misuse -> abort) | codecs.c:23 | |\n36\t| G1-002 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len = SIZE_MAX` (upper clause of same test) | `SIGABRT` (sodium_misuse) | codecs.c:23 | |\n37\t| G1-003 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `hex_maxlen <= bin_len * 2U` with no room for the NUL, e.g. `bin_len=4, hex_maxlen=8` | `SIGABRT` (sodium_misuse) | codecs.c:23 | |\n38\t| G1-004 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=0, hex_maxlen=0` (0 <= 0 is true, so even the empty case needs 1 byte) | `SIGABRT` (sodium_misuse) | codecs.c:23 | |\n39\t| G1-005 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=1, hex_maxlen=2` | `SIGABRT` (sodium_misuse) | codecs.c:23 | |\n40\t| G1-006 | `sodium_hex2bin` | output buffer full: `bin_maxlen=1, hex=\"0011\", hex_len=4, ignore=NULL, hex_end!=NULL` | returns `-1`, `errno=ERANGE`, `*bin_len=0`, `*hex_end=&hex[2]` | codecs.c:71-74 | |\n41\t| G1-007 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `bin_maxlen=0, hex=\"00\", hex_len=2, hex_end!=NULL` (fails on the very first nibble pair) | returns `-1`, `errno=ERANGE`, `*bin_len=0`, `*hex_end=&hex[0]` | codecs.c:71-74 | |\n42\t| G1-008 | `sodium_hex2bin` | same ERANGE case but `hex_end=NULL`: `bin_maxlen=1, hex=\"0011\", hex_len=4` | returns `-1`, but `errno` is overwritten to `EINVAL` by the hex_end==NULL branch, `*bin_len=0` | codecs.c:71-74 then 94-96 | |\n43\t| G1-009 | `sodium_hex2bin` | odd number of hex digits: `hex=\"abc\", hex_len=3, bin_maxlen=2, hex_end!=NULL` | returns `-1`, `errno=EINVAL`, `*bin_len=0`, `hex_pos` decremented so `*hex_end=&hex[2]` | codecs.c:84-88 | |\n44\t| G1-010 | `sodium_hex2bin` |