 the all-zero and all-`0xff` inputs.\n* **8 of the 9 `sodium_misuse()` sites in `stream_chacha20.c` are unreachable on x86-64.** The one reachable guard is `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor_ic`: `ic + ceil(mlen/64) > 2^32` — smallest case `mlen = 65, ic = 0xffffffff`. Also `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf(clen > 64*(2^32-1))` aborts on the length alone (no buffer touched). Test both out of process. Note that `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_ext_xor_ic` has **no** such guard.\n* **`crypto_ipcrypt_*` entry points are all `void`, with zero rejection branches.** The `pfx`/`ndx` variants have an IPv4-mapped-vs-IPv6 path split and a degenerate-key branch (`k[0..16] == k[16..32]` → re-expand from `k XOR 0x5a`) — exercise both a random key and a degenerate key, and both IPv4-mapped and native IPv6 16-byte inputs.\n* **Absent API** (do not invent): no `crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform`, no `_from_string_ro`, no `crypto_core_ristretto255_from_string_nu`. Only what `nm -D` shows exists.\n* `crypto_core_h2c` (`core_h2c.c`): an out-of-range `hash_alg` gives `errno = EINVAL; return -1`. `ctx_len > 0xff` is NOT an error — it selects a different DST-derivation path. Test both.\n* Point/scalar shapes to use for ed25519/ristretto255: all-zero, `01 00..00`, `ec ff..ff 7f`, `ff`×32, `00`×31 + `80`, the documented small-order points, `L-1`, `L`, `L+1`, and many random valid points obtained from `crypto_core_*_random` / `_scalarmult_base`.\n\n## Method (iterate until green)\n1. Write the Phase B file; `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test t18_core_scalarmult_kem 2>&1 | tail -40`.\n2. Fix failures. **The C is ALWAYS right — never edit anything under `c_src/`.** On divergence read the C and fix the Rust under `src/crypto_core/`, `src/crypto_scalarmult/`, `src/crypto_stream/`, `src/crypto_kem/`, `src/crypto_ipcrypt/`. Re-run until green.\n3. Same for `--test t19_core_errors`.\n4. Finally `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features 2>&1 | tail -40` to confirm nothing else broke.\n\n## Rules\n* Only create/modify: `$ROOT/tests/t18_core_scalarmult_kem.rs`, `$ROOT/tests/t19_core_errors.rs`, and files under `$ROOT/src/crypto_core/`, `$ROOT/src/crypto_scalarmult/`, `$ROOT/src/crypto_stream/`, `$ROOT/src/crypto_kem/`, `$ROOT/src/crypto_ipcrypt/` (bug fixes only). Do NOT touch `tests/common/mod.rs`, other tests, `Cargo.toml`, or anything in `c_src/`.\n* Use `timeout` on every command; keep individual tests under ~60 s (ML-KEM and ed25519 inversion are not cheap — size the input grids accordingly).\n\n## Report back\n* Exact paths + line counts of the two files, and the number of `#[test]`s in each.\n* **Every C/Rust divergence found and the exact fix made** (file + what was wrong). Most important part — pay special attention to `softaes.rs`.\n* Which G6 rows you could not construct, and why.\n* Final `cargo test` summary lines.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-rAO86K-translated-rust/d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77/tasks/a1250c3da71ff5b5f.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
