{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qtokozvub6eew2ksf26zq7xk765dsiexnyvjmmrxuxzrzhmqeovq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_014UNtAYri5t489phSRr2y9D","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase C tests: hashes/MACs/XOFs/KDFs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing **differential tests** that verify a Rust translation of **libsodium 1.0.23** matches the C reference byte-for-byte, for ONE module group.\n\nROOT = `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust` (crate root, your cwd)\n\n## Read these FIRST\n1. `$ROOT/.phaseA/HARNESS.md` — the test-harness contract. Follow it exactly.\n2. `$ROOT/tests/common/mod.rs` — the harness implementation.\n3. `$ROOT/tests/t03_hashes.rs` — the EXISTING Phase B test for your group. It already covers: sha256/sha512/sha3256/sha3512 (one-shot + streaming with random chunking), blake2b/generichash (one-shot + streaming + `salt_personal` + `init_salt_personal`), poly1305 (one-shot + streaming + verify), the four XOFs (one-shot, `_init`/`_update`/`_squeeze` streaming, `_init_with_domain` over all 256 domain bytes), `crypto_core_keccak1600` (randomised operation programs), `crypto_kdf[_blake2b]_derive_from_key`, hkdf sha256/sha512 (`_extract`, `_expand`, streaming `_extract_init/_update/_final`) and the keygens. **Do NOT duplicate that coverage.**\n4. `$ROOT/tests/t05_aead_errors.rs` — worked Phase C example, including the out-of-process `sodium_misuse`/`assert` pattern.\n5. `$ROOT/CONFIGS.md` section **`## G4`** — 149 valid-input rows (`G4-001` … `G4-149`).\n6. `$ROOT/ERRORS.md` section **`## G4`** — 135 error rows (`G4-001` … `G4-135`). This is your MAIN job.\n\n## YOUR GROUP (G4) = hashes / MACs / XOFs / KDFs\n`crypto_generichash` (+blake2b), `crypto_hash` (sha256/sha512/sha3256/sha3512), `crypto_shorthash` (siphash24/siphashx24), `crypto_onetimeauth` (poly1305), `crypto_verify_16/32/64`, `crypto_xof_{shake128,shake256,turboshake128,turboshake256}`, `crypto_core_keccak1600`, `crypto_kdf` (+blake2b, hkdf_sha256, hkdf_sha512).\n\nRust source you MAY fix: `src/crypto_generichash/`, `src/crypto_hash/`, `src/crypto_shorthash/`, `src/crypto_onetimeauth/`, `src/crypto_verify/`, `src/crypto_xof/`, `src/crypto_kdf/`.\n**`src/crypto_core/` (incl. keccak1600) is owned by a different agent — do NOT edit it. If a divergence traces there, report it precisely instead of fixing it.**\n\n## Deliverables\n* `$ROOT/tests/t14_hash_errors.rs` — Phase C: cover EVERY row of ERRORS `## G4`. Doc-comment each `#[test]` with the `G4-NNN` ids it covers.\n* `$ROOT/tests/t15_hash_extra.rs` — Phase B gap-filling: any CONFIGS `## G4` row not already covered by `t03_hashes.rs`. Read CONFIGS `## G4` row by row, diff against `t03_hashes.rs`, and write tests for the remainder (with MANY randomised inputs, `Rng::new(<fixed seed>)`). Doc-comment the `G4-NNN` ids covered. If a row is already fully covered by `t03_hashes.rs`, note that in a comment block at the top of the file listing those ids — do not re-test it.\n\n## Critical correctness notes (verified from source — honour them)\n* **There is NO turboshake domain-byte range check.** `_init_with_domain` accepts all 256 values and returns `0`. `DOMAIN_STANDARD` is `0x1F` for all four XOFs.\n* **`crypto_xof_*` has no `_final`, `_absorb` or `_clone`.** Exports per primitive: bare name, `_init`, `_init_with_domain`, `_update`, `_squeeze`, `_statebytes`, `_blockbytes`, `_domain_standard`. Absorb == `_update`; finalisation is implicit in the first `_squeeze`. So **`_update` after `_squeeze`** is the interesting state-machine row — find out exactly what the C does and assert it.\n* **`crypto_core_keccak1600` has no `_absorb`/`_pad`/rate parameter and does ZERO bounds checking** — `offset + length > 200` is silent OOB (UB, not a rejection; note the row).\n* **SHA-3 exports only `sha3256` (rate 136) and `sha3512` (rate 72)** — no 224/384. Domain byte `0x06`. `sha3_update` after `_final` returns `-1` **but still permutes the state and resets `offset`** — a very easy thing to get wrong; test `_final` then `_update` then `_final` and compare both digests.\n* **`crypto_generichash_BYTES_MIN`/`KEYBYTES_MIN` (16) are NOT enforced** — `outlen = 1` and `keylen = 1` both return `0`. Only `1 <= outlen <= 64` and `keylen <= 64` are checked.\n* **`_final` does NOT validate `outlen` against the `outlen` passed to `_init`** — `_init(...,32)` then `_final(...,64)` returns `0`.\n* **Three DIFFERENT outcomes for `crypto_generichash[_blake2b]_final`'s `outlen`:** `outlen == 0` → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT; `outlen` in 65..=255 → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT; `outlen >= 256` → **failed `assert()`** → SIGABRT (different mechanism, different stderr). Meanwhile `_init` and the one-shot return `-1` for those same values. Test all of it; use the out-of-process pattern for the abort rows and remember an `assert` abort does NOT go through the misuse handler (so it dies with signal 6, not exit 77) — assert C and Rust agree on the signal.\n* **Key-NULL asymmetry:** `crypto_generichash(out,32,in,1,NULL,5)` → SIGABRT, but `crypto_generichash_init(state,NULL,5,32)` → returns `0` (silently unkeyed). Test both.\n* **hkdf's only abort path:** `_extract` / `_extract_init` with `salt == NULL && salt_len > 0` → `sodium_misuse()`/SIGABRT (via `crypto_auth_hmacsha*_init`).\n* `crypto_kdf_hkdf_sha256_BYTES_MAX = 8160`, `_sha512 = 16320`, both `BYTES_MIN = 0`. `_expand` with `out_len > BYTES_MAX` must reject identically.\n* `crypto_kdf[_blake2b]_derive_from_key` with `subkey_len` below `BYTES_MIN` or above `BYTES_MAX`.\n* poly1305 uses `poly1305_donna32.h` (no `HAVE_TI_MODE`); blake2b uses the ref compress; `crypto_verify_n` uses the portable `volatile uint16_t` loop.\n* Also cover generic-wrapper rejections: `crypto_generichash`, `crypto_hash`, `crypto_shorthash`, `crypto_onetimeauth`, `crypto_kdf` dispatchers.\n\n## Method (iterate until green)\n1. Write `t14_hash_errors.rs`; `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test t14_hash_errors 2>&1 | tail -40`. Fix failures. **The C is ALWAYS right — never edit anything under `c_src/`.**\n2. Write `t15_hash_extra.rs`; `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test t15_hash_extra 2>&1 | tail -40`. Fix failures.\n3. Finally `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features 2>&1 | tail -40` to confirm nothing else broke. Other agents are editing other `src/` subtrees concurrently, so if you see a failure in a test file you did not write and it is not in your subtree, just report it — do not fix it.\n\n## Rules\n* Only create/modify: `$ROOT/tests/t14_hash_errors.rs`, `$ROOT/tests/t15_hash_extra.rs`, and files under the seven `src/` directories listed above. Do NOT touch `tests/common/mod.rs`, other test files, `Cargo.toml`, `src/crypto_core/`, or anything in `c_src/`.\n* Use `timeout` on every command; keep individual tests under ~60 s.\n\n## Report back\n* Exact paths + line counts of the two files, and the number of `#[test]`s in each.\n* **Every C/Rust divergence found and the exact fix made** (file + what was wrong). Most important part.\n* Any divergence that traced into `src/crypto_core/` (report, don't fix).\n* Which G4 rows you could not construct, and why.\n* Final `cargo test` summary lines."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10863,"cache_read_input_tokens":272490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10863,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"cdf62a8e-0d4d-41b7-8b60-8d29d7807961","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:29:03.364Z"}
