rables\n* `$ROOT/tests/t16_box_sign.rs` — Phase B, covering every CONFIGS `## G5` row with MANY randomised inputs per row (`Rng::new(<fixed seed>)`). Doc-comment each `#[test]` with the `G5-NNN` ids it covers.\n* `$ROOT/tests/t17_box_sign_errors.rs` — Phase C, covering EVERY row of ERRORS `## G5`. Doc-comment each `#[test]` with the `G5-NNN` ids it covers.\n\n## Coverage that MUST be present (these are the \"low-level entry point\" requirements)\n* **crypto_box — all four API layers, for BOTH primitives** (`curve25519xsalsa20poly1305` = default, and `curve25519xchacha20poly1305`):\n  (a) NaCl API `crypto_box` / `crypto_box_open` / `_beforenm` / `_afternm` / `_open_afternm` with the `ZEROBYTES`/`BOXZEROBYTES` zero-padding convention — you must actually build the padded buffers correctly;\n  (b) easy API `_easy` / `_open_easy` / `_easy_afternm` / `_open_easy_afternm`;\n  (c) detached API `_detached` / `_open_detached` / `_detached_afternm` / `_open_detached_afternm`;\n  (d) sealed boxes `_seal` / `_seal_open`.\n  Note the API-surface asymmetry confirmed against `nm -D`: `curve25519xchacha20poly1305` has **no** NaCl combined/afternm API and no `ZEROBYTES`/`BOXZEROBYTES`; `curve25519xsalsa20poly1305` has the NaCl layer under its explicit name, but its easy/detached/seal layers exist only under the generic `crypto_box_*` names. Do not invent symbols — check `nm` first.\n* **crypto_secretbox** — NaCl `crypto_secretbox`/`_open`, easy `_easy`/`_open_easy`, detached `_detached`/`_open_detached`, for BOTH `xsalsa20poly1305` and `xchacha20poly1305`.\n* **crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305** — `_keygen`/`_init_push`/`_push`/`_init_pull`/`_pull`/`_rekey`, tag ∈ {MESSAGE 0, PUSH 1, REKEY 2, FINAL 3}, adlen ∈ {0,1,16,100}, mlen ∈ {0,1,16,17,63,64,65,1000}, multi-message streams (2/3/10 messages), explicit mid-stream `_rekey`, and `mlen_p`/`clen_p`/`tag_p` NULL vs non-NULL.\n* **crypto_sign_ed25519** — `_keypair` vs `_seed_keypair`, combined `crypto_sign`/`_open` vs `_detached`/`_verify_detached`, the multipart ed25519ph API (`_init`/`_update` chunked/`_final_create`/`_final_verify`), and the conversions `_sk_to_seed`/`_sk_to_pk`/`_pk_to_curve25519`/`_sk_to_curve25519`.\n* **crypto_kx** — `_keypair`/`_seed_keypair`/`_client_session_keys`/`_server_session_keys`, with `rx`/`tx` NULL vs non-NULL (verify from the source which are allowed), and the client/server key agreement actually matching.\n* **crypto_auth** — `hmacsha256`, `hmacsha512`, `hmacsha512256`, one-shot vs `_init`/`_update`(chunked)/`_final`, key lengths {0,1,32,64,65,128,129,200} (a key longer than the HMAC block size is hashed first — a distinct branch), inlen {0,1,63,64,65,127,128,129,1000}, `_verify` correct and incorrect.\n* Message lengths throughout: {0,1,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,1000} at minimum.\n\n## Critical correctness notes (verified from source — honour them)\n* `ED25519_COMPAT` and `ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC` are **never defined**: signing is fully deterministic (does NOT consult `randombytes`), and verification uses the canonical-S + `ge25519_is_canonical(pk)` branch (there is NO legacy `sig[63] & 224` check).\n* There is **no runtime `assert()` and no `abort()`** in G5. The only abort path is `sodium_misuse()`.\n* **`crypto_sign_ed25519_open` zeroes `m` on signature failure but NOT on the `smlen < 64` path**; `*mlen_p = 0` on both. All `*_open_detached` MAC failures leave `m` **completely untouched**. Assert these exactly with `canary()` buffers.\n* **`crypto_secretstream_..._pull` writes `*mlen_p = 0` and `*tag_p = 0xff` BEFORE any validation**, so those stores are observable on every failure path. It does **not** validate the decrypted tag byte, and pushing after `TAG_FINAL` still succeeds (returns 0). Its message-padding formula reduces to `mlen & 0xf` (the in-source comment flags it as a bug) — the Rust must reproduce it exactly.\n* **`crypto_box_seal` still `memcpy`s the ephemeral pk into `c[0..32]` even when the inner `crypto_box_easy` fails.**\n* **`crypto_auth_hmacsha{256,512}_init` with `key == NULL` and `keylen > blocksize` bypasses the `sodium_misuse` guard → NULL deref / SIGSEGV**, not a clean abort. Test it out of process and assert C and Rust die the same way.\n* **`crypto_secretbox_detached` chunks the encrypt path at `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072` while `_open_detached` does not**; the xchacha20 variant chunks in neither direction. So test `mlen` = 131071 / 131072 / 131073 / 262144 for both.\n* `crypto_box_beforenm` rejects small-order / all-zero peer public keys (via `crypto_scalarmult` returning -1). Concrete rejected pks: `00`×32, `01 00…00`, `ec ff..ff 7f`, `00`×31+`80`, and the documented small-order points.\n* Concrete ed25519 rejection inputs (verified at runtime): non-canonical pk `ed ff..ff 7f`, `ee ff..ff 7f`, `ff`×32; decompression failure `02 00…00`, `07 00…00`, `08 00…00`; small-order pk `00`×32, `01 00…00`, `ec ff..ff 7f`, `00`×31+`80`; non-canonical S = `L`, `L+1`, `ff`×32 (note `L-1` IS canonical). `L` = `edd3f55c1a631258d69cf7a2def9de1400000000000000000000000000000010` little-endian.\n* `_pk_to_curve25519` has THREE distinct `return -1` branches (non-canonical, has-small-order, off-the-main-subgroup) — construct one input for each. Off-subgroup-but-valid pks: `03/04/05/06/09/0a 00…00`, `ff`×32.\n\n## Method (iterate until green)\n1. Write the Phase B file; `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features --test t16_box_sign 2>&1 | tail -40`. Fix failures. **The C is ALWAYS right — never edit anything under `c_src/`.**\n2. Same for `--test t17_box_sign_errors`.\n3. Finally `timeout 600 cargo test --no-default-features 2>&1 | tail -40`. Other agents are editing other `src/` subtrees concurrently, so if a test you did not write fails outside your subtree, report it rather than fixing it.\n\n## Rules\n* Only create/modify: `$ROOT/tests/t16_box_sign.rs`, `$ROOT/tests/t17_box_sign_errors.rs`, and files under the six `src/` directories you own. Do NOT touch `tests/common/mod.rs`, other test files, `Cargo.toml`, the other agents' `src/` subtrees, or anything in `c_src/`.\n* Use `timeout` on every command; keep individual tests under ~60 s.\n\n## Report back\n* Exact paths + line counts of the two files, and the number of `#[test]`s in each.\n* **Every C/Rust divergence found and the exact fix made** (file + what was wrong). Most important part.\n* Any divergence that traced into another agent's subtree (report, don't fix).\n* Which G5 rows you could not construct, and why.\n* Final `cargo test` summary lines.","uuid":"fcce32dc-1327-4767-b7fb-291f16d2ee2f","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77"}
