{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FtkbRPEUYsv5ds9Dudgb25","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `crypto_box/crypto_box_seal.c`.\n2\t\n3\tuse core::ffi::{c_int, c_void};\n4\t\n5\tuse crate::sodium::core::sodium_misuse;\n6\tuse crate::sodium::utils::sodium_memzero;\n7\t\n8\tuse super::easy::{crypto_box_easy, crypto_box_open_easy};\n9\tuse super::{\n10\t    crypto_box_NONCEBYTES, crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES, crypto_box_SEALBYTES,\n11\t    crypto_box_SECRETKEYBYTES, crypto_box_keypair,\n12\t};\n13\t\n14\t/// ABI-compatible stand-in for `crypto_generichash_state`\n15\t/// (`typedef crypto_generichash_blake2b_state`, i.e.\n16\t/// `struct CRYPTO_ALIGN(64) { unsigned char opaque[384]; }`).\n17\t#[repr(C, align(64))]\n18\tstruct crypto_generichash_state {\n19\t    opaque: [u8; 384],\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\t// Defined in crypto_generichash/crypto_generichash.c.\n23\tunsafe extern \"C\" {\n24\t    fn crypto_generichash_init(\n25\t        state: *mut crypto_generichash_state,\n26\t        key: *const u8,\n27\t        keylen: usize,\n28\t        outlen: usize,\n29\t    ) -> c_int;\n30\t    fn crypto_generichash_update(\n31\t        state: *mut crypto_generichash_state,\n32\t        in_: *const u8,\n33\t        inlen: u64,\n34\t    ) -> c_int;\n35\t    fn crypto_generichash_final(\n36\t        state: *mut crypto_generichash_state,\n37\t        out: *mut u8,\n38\t        outlen: usize,\n39\t    ) -> c_int;\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tunsafe fn _crypto_box_seal_nonce(\n43\t    nonce: *mut u8,\n44\t    pk1: *const u8,\n45\t    pk2: *const u8,\n46\t) -> c_int {\n47\t    unsafe {\n48\t        let mut st = crypto_generichash_state { opaque: [0; 384] };\n49\t\n50\t        crypto_generichash_init(&mut st, core::ptr::null(), 0, crypto_box_NONCEBYTES);\n51\t        crypto_generichash_update(&mut st, pk1, crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES as u64);\n52\t        crypto_generichash_update(&mut st, pk2, crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES as u64);\n53\t        crypto_generichash_final(&mut st, nonce, crypto_box_NONCEBYTES);\n54\t\n55\t        0\n56\t    }\n57\t}\n58\t\n59\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n60\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn crypto_box_seal(\n61\t    c: *mut u8,\n62\t    m: *const u8,\n63\t    mlen: u64,\n64\t    pk: *const u8,\n65\t) -> c_int {\n66\t    unsafe {\n67\t        let mut nonce: [u8; crypto_box_NONCEBYTES] = [0; crypto_box_NONCEBYTES];\n68\t        let mut epk: [u8; crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES] = [0; crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES];\n69\t        let mut esk: [u8; crypto_box_SECRETKEYBYTES] = [0; crypto_box_SECRETKEYBYTES];\n70\t        let ret: c_int;\n71\t\n72\t        if mlen > crate::crypto_box::crypto_box_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX as u64 {\n73\t            sodium_misuse(); /* LCOV_EXCL_LINE */\n74\t        }\n75\t        if crypto_box_keypair(epk.as_mut_ptr(), esk.as_mut_ptr()) != 0 {\n76\t            return -1; /* LCOV_EXCL_LINE */\n77\t        }\n78\t        _crypto_box_seal_nonce(nonce.as_mut_ptr(), epk.as_ptr(), pk);\n79\t        ret = crypto_box_easy(\n80\t            c.add(crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES),\n81\t            m,\n82\t            mlen,\n83\t            nonce.as_ptr(),\n84\t            pk,\n85\t            esk.as_ptr(),\n86\t        );\n87\t        core::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(epk.as_ptr(), c, crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES);\n88\t        sodium_memzero(esk.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void, core::mem::size_of_val(&esk));\n89\t\n90\t        ret\n91\t    }\n92\t}\n93\t\n94\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n95\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn crypto_box_seal_open(\n96\t    m: *mut u8,\n97\t    c: *const u8,\n98\t    clen: u64,\n99\t    pk: *const u8,\n100\t    sk: *const u8,\n101\t) -> c_int {\n102\t    unsafe {\n103\t        let mut nonce: [u8; crypto_box_NONCEBYTES] = [0; crypto_box_NONCEBYTES];\n104\t\n105\t        if clen < crypto_box_SEALBYTES as u64 {\n106\t            return -1;\n107\t        }\n108\t        _crypto_box_seal_nonce(nonce.as_mut_ptr(), c, pk);\n109\t\n110\t        // COMPILER_ASSERT(crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES < crypto_box_SEALBYTES);\n111\t        const _: () = assert!(crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES < crypto_box_SEALBYTES);\n112\t        crypto_box_open_easy(\n113\t            m,\n114\t            c.add(crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES),\n115\t            clen - crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES as u64,\n116\t            nonce.as_ptr(),\n117\t            c,\n118\t            sk,\n119\t        )\n120\t    }\n121\t}\n122\t\n123\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n124\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn crypto_box_sealbytes() -> usize {\n125\t    crypto_box_SEALBYTES\n126\t}\n127\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X99zS24Fq89wn6vCQ5taZZ","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"f5616200-d8c0-4aea-836e-b05337bc01b8","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:32:06.416Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Review crypto_box/secretbox Rust vs C"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yfxyp4levkydqvxozf5hzwpd6crj6b32laiulo65bougsv6whncq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01AWhB5J94zFJgcRQe6qXZB4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review sign/auth Rust vs C","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust\n\nThis repo is a Rust translation of libsodium 1.0.23. The C reference is under `c_src/libsodium/`, the Rust port under `src/`.\n\nYour task: read the following C files and their Rust counterparts LINE BY LINE and report EVERY semantic divergence (behaviour, return value, out-parameter writes, order of operations, buffer zeroing, arithmetic, length guards, off-by-one, wrapping).\n\nC files:\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/crypto_sign.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/sign_ed25519.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/ref10/keypair.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/ref10/open.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/ref10/sign.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_auth/crypto_auth.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_auth/hmacsha256/auth_hmacsha256.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_auth/hmacsha512/auth_hmacsha512.c\n- c_src/libsodium/crypto_auth/hmacsha512256/auth_hmacsha512256.c\n\nRust files:\n- src/crypto_sign/**/*.rs\n- src/crypto_auth/*.rs\n\nPay special attention to:\n1. Neither `ED25519_COMPAT` nor `ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC` is defined. So the `#else` branches are active: verify does `if ((sig[63] & 240) != 0 && sc25519_is_canonical(sig+32) == 0) return -1;` then `if (ge25519_is_canonical(pk) == 0) return -1;`. There is NO `sig[63] & 224` check. Signing is deterministic and does NOT call randombytes.\n2. `crypto_sign_ed25519_open`: on the `smlen < 64` path it does NOT memset `m`, only `*mlen_p = 0`; on the verify-failure path it DOES `memset(m, 0, smlen-64)` when `m != NULL`, then `*mlen_p = 0`. Both return -1.\n3. `crypto_sign_ed25519` does `memmove(sm+64, m, mlen)` BEFORE signing, so `sm[64..]` is always written, and signs over `sm+64` (not `m`).\n4. `crypto_sign_ed25519_seed_keypair`: hashes seed into `sk` (64 bytes of SHA-512 written into sk!), clamps sk[0]/sk[31], scalarmult_base, then `memmove(sk, seed, 32)` and `memmove(sk+32, pk, 32)`. So sk = seed || pk.\n5. `crypto_sign_ed25519_pk_to_curve25519` has THREE `return -1` conditions ORed: frombytes_negate_vartime != 0, has_small_order != 0, is_on_main_subgroup == 0. It does NOT call ge25519_is_canonical.\n6. `_crypto_sign_ed25519_detached` order: hinit(prehashed); sha512(az, sk, 32); update(az+32,32); update(m,mlen); final(nonce); `memmove(sig+32, sk+32, 32)`; sc25519_reduce(nonce); scalarmult_base; p3_tobytes(sig); hinit again; update(sig,64); update(m,mlen); final(hram); reduce; clamp(az); sc25519_muladd(sig+32, hram, az, nonce). Note `sig[32..64]` is temporarily the pk.\n7. ed25519ph: `_final_create`/`_final_verify` call `crypto_hash_sha512_final` (which zeroes the state!) then delegate with prehashed=1. The dom2 prefix is 34 bytes: \"SigEd25519 no Ed25519 collisions\" + 0x01 0x00.\n8. hmacsha256_init: `if (keylen > 64) { hash key into khash; key = khash; keylen = 32; } else if (key == NULL) { if (keylen > 0) sodium_misuse(); }`. NOTE: with key==NULL and keylen>64, the FIRST branch is taken so `crypto_hash_sha256_update(&ictx, NULL, keylen)` is a NULL deref → SIGSEGV, NOT a clean misuse. The Rust must behave the same way (segfault).\n9. hmacsha512 threshold is 128, not 64.\n10. hmacsha512256 is a thin forwarder to hmacsha512 with truncation to 32 bytes only in `_final`; the state types are the same typedef.\n11. `crypto_auth_hmacsha*_verify` returns `crypto_verify_N(h, correct) | (-(h == correct)) | sodium_memcmp(correct, h, N)`. The `-(h==correct)` term is always 0.\n12. `_final` zeroes the sha state (sodium_memzero in crypto_hash_sha*_final), so a second `_final` on the same state operates on a zeroed state.\n13. statebytes: hmacsha256 = 208, hmacsha512 = 416, hmacsha512256 = 416, crypto_sign_state = 208.\n\nReport findings as a concise numbered list: `src/<file>:<line>` — what the Rust does — what the C does. Do NOT edit any file. Be precise and exhaustive; if you find no divergence in a file say so explicitly."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":173794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":657,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018AKqc9oZCiiirxxs7Qyssn","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"262484c9-afeb-4f8f-b54d-9ca884418ec9","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:32:06.997Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B+C tests: box/secretbox/sign/kx/auth"}
