terminator | result is the empty string, returns `hex`; codecs.c:26-38 | | [ ] |\n| G1-002 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=1`, `bin={0x00}`, `hex_maxlen=3` -> `\"00\"` (exercises the `c < 10` digit branch of the `87U + c + (((c-10U)>>8) & ~38U)` expression) | codecs.c:29-33 | | [ ] |\n| G1-003 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=1`, `bin={0x0a}`, `hex_maxlen=3` -> `\"0a\"` (low nibble >= 10 -> letter branch) | codecs.c:29-33 | | [ ] |\n| G1-004 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=1`, `bin={0xff}` -> `\"ff\"`; `bin={0xa0}` -> `\"a0\"` (both nibbles >= 10) | output is ALWAYS lowercase; codecs.c:29-33 | | [ ] |\n| G1-005 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=2`, `hex_maxlen=5` (exact fit) vs `hex_maxlen=64` (oversized) | with an oversized buffer only `bin_len*2+1` bytes are written; the rest of `hex` is left UNTOUCHED (contrast with `sodium_bin2base64`, which zero-fills); codecs.c:36 | | [ ] |\n| G1-006 | `sodium_bin2hex` | `bin_len=32` (typical key), `hex_maxlen=65`; and `bin_len=1024`, `hex_maxlen=2049` | linear loop, no size-specific branches; codecs.c:26-35 | | [ ] |\n| G1-007 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `hex_len=0`, `bin_maxlen=0`, `ignore=NULL`, `bin_len!=NULL`, `hex_end=NULL` | returns `0`, `*bin_len=0`; the empty input is valid; codecs.c:57, 92-100 | | [ ] |\n| G1-008 | `sodium_hex2bin` | even lowercase input `hex=\"00ff\"`, `bin_maxlen=2`, `ignore=NULL`, `hex_end=NULL`, `bin_len!=NULL` | returns `0`, 2 bytes; codecs.c:57-83 | | [ ] |\n| G1-009 | `sodium_hex2bin` | UPPERCASE input `hex=\"00FF\"` (the `(c & ~32U) - 55U` alpha path) | accepted, same bytes as lowercase; codecs.c:61-62 | | [ ] |\n| G1-010 | `sodium_hex2bin` | MIXED case `hex=\"AbCd\"` | accepted -> `{0xab,0xcd}`; codecs.c:61-62 | | [ ] |\n| G1-011 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `ignore=\":\"`, `hex=\"00:11:22\"`, `hex_len=8`, `bin_maxlen=3`, `hex_end=NULL` | returns `0`, 3 bytes; separators consumed only at byte boundaries; codecs.c:64-67 | | [ ] |\n| G1-012 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `ignore=\": \\n\"`, `hex=\"00 11\\n22\"` (multiple distinc