s.c:57-83 | | [ ] |\n| G1-023 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | `variant=1 (ORIGINAL)` x `bin_len=0,1,2,3,4,5,6` -> `1,5,5,5,9,9,9` (includes the trailing NUL) | macro `sodium_base64_ENCODED_LEN`; utils.h:79-88, codecs.c:181 | | [ ] |\n| G1-024 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | `variant=3 (ORIGINAL_NO_PADDING)` x `bin_len=0,1,2,3,4,5,6` -> `1,3,4,5,7,8,9` | the `(VARIANT & 2)` term removes the padding allowance; utils.h:79-88 | | [ ] |\n| G1-025 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | `variant=5 (URLSAFE)` x `bin_len=1,2,3` -> `5,5,5` (identical to ORIGINAL: the URLSAFE bit does not affect length) | utils.h:79-88 | | [ ] |\n| G1-026 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | `variant=7 (URLSAFE_NO_PADDING)` x `bin_len=1,2,3` -> `3,4,5` | utils.h:79-88 | | [ ] |\n| G1-027 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | large valid value: `bin_len=1000000, variant=1` and `variant=3` | pure arithmetic, no allocation; codecs.c:173-182 | | [ ] |\n| G1-028 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | exactly one below the misuse threshold: `bin_len=0xBFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC` | returns a huge size_t without aborting (threshold is `bin_len/3 > (SIZE_MAX-5)/4`); codecs.c:178 | | [ ] |\n| G1-029 | `sodium_bin2base64` | `variant=1`, `bin_len=0`, `b64_maxlen=1` | empty string; `b64_len=0`, one NUL written; codecs.c:198-247 | | [ ] |\n===== ERRORS\n# ERRORS.md — the ERROR-SURFACE TABLE (Phase A / gate for Phase C)\n\nMechanically derived from the C source in `c_src/libsodium`: **every** distinct\nway the library rejects or errors on input — every `return -1` / `return NULL` /\nerror-enum return, every `sodium_misuse()` (which runs the installed handler and\nthen `abort()`s → SIGABRT), every active `assert()`, every explicit range / bounds\n/ overflow check, every NULL check the code itself performs, every `errno = ...`\nassignment, and every out-of-range enum / `alg` / variant value.\n\nBuild configuration these rows describe (see `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`): **no `HAVE_*`\nmacros** and **no `NDEBUG`** — so every `#ifdef HAVE_*` selects the