{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_il2aahdtcmbrauxpm6gwxjc5moccnwuvnge5ii66jpjf7p6sowna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read all 10 C files and all 10 Rust files line by line, plus the relevant headers (`crypto_box.h`, `crypto_box_curve25519xsalsa20poly1305.h`, `crypto_box_curve25519xchacha20poly1305.h`, `crypto_secretbox*.h`, `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305.h`, `crypto_generichash_blake2b.h`, `private/common.h`) and the helpers (`src/common.rs` `memmove`/`SODIUM_SIZE_MAX`, `src/sodium/utils.rs` `sodium_memzero`, `src/sodium/core.rs` `sodium_misuse`).\n\n## Result: no semantic divergences found.\n\nEvery one of the 10 pairs is a faithful translation. Explicitly, per file:\n\n1. `src/crypto_box/mod.rs` (vs `crypto_box.c`) — no divergence. All 10 accessors, `crypto_box_primitive()` (`\"curve25519xsalsa20poly1305\\0\"`, 27 bytes), and all 7 delegating wrappers match. Constants match the header: SEED/PK/SK/BEFORENM = 32, NONCE = 24, MAC = BOXZERO = 16, ZERO = 32, SEAL = 48, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = `SODIUM_SIZE_MAX - 16`.\n2. `src/crypto_box/easy.rs` (vs `crypto_box_easy.c`) — no divergence. `sodium_misuse()` guard present in `_easy_afternm` (line 80) and `_easy` (line 97), correctly **absent** from `_detached`/`_detached_afternm`. `clen < 16 -> -1` present in `_open_easy_afternm` (line 149) and `_open_easy` (line 173), absent from `_open_detached*`. Both `_detached`/`_open_detached` zero `k` only after the inner call and return `ret`, returning `-1` early (without zeroing) on `beforenm` failure — matching C. `COMPILER_ASSERT(BEFORENMBYTES >= crypto_secretbox_KEYBYTES)` is a `const _: () = assert!(...)` in `_detached` only, as in C.\n3. `src/crypto_box/seal.rs` (vs `crypto_box_seal.c`) — no divergence. `crypto_box_seal` line 87 does the `epk -> c[0..32]` copy **unconditionally**, after `crypto_box_easy`, before `sodium_memzero(esk)`, and returns the saved `ret` — exactly the C behaviour when the inner ea