{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rjktppfz57hx42jbkqvdvmo7hl6kqfg5e7tb56yxmssjkxhdjmzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_017MNfTt5bQ6gBMm7Yq58dSG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='CONFIGS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor = \"## Row counts\\n\"\nsec = \"\"\"## Build-time configuration surface (feature combinations)\n\n`Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` table at all**, and `grep -rn 'cfg(feature'\nsrc/ tests/` finds **0 matches**. The power set of declared features therefore has\nexactly **one** element — the empty set — so `--no-default-features` and the plain\ndefault build are the same single configuration:\n\n| # | cargo invocation | features | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `cargo check/test --no-default-features` | (none) | OK |\n| 1' | `cargo check/test` (default) | (none) | OK — identical to #1 |\n\nEnumerated and verified automatically by `.phaseA/feature_matrix.sh`, which reads\nthe feature names out of `Cargo.toml`, builds their power set, and runs\n`cargo check` / `cargo test` for each element (so it stays correct if features are\never added):\n\n```sh\n$ .phaseA/feature_matrix.sh check\n=== Build-time configuration surface ===\nCargo [features] declared : 0 (none)\ndefault feature set       : (none)\ncfg(feature = ...) in src : 0 files\n\n=== 1 feature combination(s) to verify ===\nOK: <no features>\nOK: default\n```\n\nThe only `#[cfg]` gates in `src/` are architecture gates\n(`target_arch = \"x86_64\" | \"aarch64\" | \"x86\" | \"arm\"` and the portable\n`not(any(...))` fallback) plus one `cfg(test)`. They are selected by the target\ntriple, not by a Cargo feature, so they do not multiply the combination count on\na fixed target (x86-64 Linux here).\n\nThe **C** side has an analogous single configuration: `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`\ndefines **no `HAVE_*` macros** and passes no `-DNDEBUG`\n(`C_DEFINES = -Dsodium_EXPORTS`, `C_FLAGS = -fPIC -std=gnu99`), so every\n`#ifdef HAVE_*` takes the portable branch (`ref` / `ref10` / `soft` / `nosse` /\n`donna32` / `fe_25_5`) and `assert()` is live. The Rust crate reproduces exactly\nthat configuration, which is why one Cargo configuration suffices.\n\n\"\"\"\nassert anchor in s\ns = s.replace(anchor, sec + anchor, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"inserted\")\nPY\ngrep -n 'Build-time configuration surface' CONFIGS.md","description":"Document feature surface in CONFIGS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":400241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"f378f980-7cfb-4446-a208-9bf24a4e69ac","timestamp":"2026-08-23T08:41:27.461Z"}
