{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sbjdaa737njy5obfuzq44onyrwwtwltn6u2ibvoblcz2es4vyanq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both G6 differential-test files are written and green, and **no Rust source changes were needed** — the G6 translation matched the C byte-for-byte on every input I could construct.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n| file | lines | `#[test]`s |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t18_core_scalarmult_kem.rs` | 3766 | 37 |\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t19_core_errors.rs` | 2542 | 27 |\n\nRow coverage is complete and machine-checked: every one of CONFIGS `## G6` **G6-001 … G6-173** and ERRORS `## G6` **G6-001 … G6-149** appears verbatim in a doc comment. The t18 header carries an explicit row map for the rows already driven by `t02_lowlevel.rs`/`t01_constants.rs` (chacha/salsa `_xor`/`_xor_ic` sweeps, the `crypto_core_salsa*`/`_hsalsa20`/`_hchacha20` matrix, the pure constant accessors) so nothing looks dropped.\n\n## C/Rust divergences found: **none**\n\nNothing under `src/crypto_core/`, `src/crypto_scalarmult/`, `src/crypto_stream/`, `src/crypto_kem/`, `src/crypto_ipcrypt/` was modified. Specifically on the flagged risks:\n\n* **`src/crypto_core/softaes.rs` is correct.** It translates the **SRM-1R bitsliced `#else` branch**, not the `FAVOR_PERFORMANCE` 1024-entry-LUT half (which is indeed compiled out). I verified this *directly* rather than only through ipcrypt: the internal aliases `_sodium_softaes_expand_key128/256`, `_invert_key_schedule128/256`, `_inv_mix_columns`, `_block_encrypt/_decrypt/_encryptlast/_decryptlast` **are exported from both `.so`s**, so `softaes_primitives` calls them through `dlsym` with a `#[repr(C)]` 4×`u32` `SoftAesBlock` passed/returned by value. All four round functions agree over 178 blocks × 10 round keys (incl. every single-bit block and the all-zero/all-0xff extremes), both key schedules agree over 64 random + 3 fixed keys, and the primitives composed by hand reproduce the FIPS-197 AES-128 vector `69c4e0d8…` in both directions (which also proves the struct ABI).\n* **`fe_25_5`**: exercised hard by a dedicated `field_arithmetic_structured_inputs` test (every canonical `y` in `0..96` and `p-96..p` with both sign bits, `2^255-1`, all 256 single-bit x25519 x-coordinates, and ristretto elligator with each 32-byte half at `0/1/2/3/p-2/p-1/p/p+1/2^255-1/2^255`).\n* **ML-KEM implicit rejection**: `_dec` asserted to return 0 *and* to produce identical C/Rust shared secrets for valid ciphertexts, 8 single-bit corruptions, all-zero/all-0xff/random ciphertexts, and all-zero/all-0xff/random secret keys.\n* **`_is_inf` reachability**: constructed via `_noclamp` with `n = L … 7L` and `n = 00..00 80` (all → identity → `-1`); the clamped forms are asserted *never* to reach it (`documented_unreachable_error_rows` sweeps 200+ scalars incl. `kL`).\n* **`_add`/`_sub` validation gap**: confirmed they accept non-canonical-but-on-curve (`ed ff..7f`, `ee ff..7f`) and all six small-order encodings while `_is_valid_point` rejects them.\n* **x25519 dead all-zero check**: all 7 blocklisted points (with and without bit 255) rejected by the first check; asserted that no successful `mult` ever yields an all-zero `q`.\n* **ChaCha20 misuse**: 8 out-of-process cases, all reaching `sodium_misuse()` (exit 77) identically in C and Rust — `_ietf(clen=max+1|u64max)`, `_ietf_xor(mlen=max+1|u64max)`, `_ietf_xor_ic` at `(65,0xffffffff)`, `(129,0xfffffffe)`, `(193,0xfffffffd)`, `(128,0xffffffff)`. `_ietf_ext_xor_ic` confirmed to have **no** guard (silent counter wrap tested).\n* **ipcrypt**: `pfx` included — both `is_ipv4_mapped` paths, both `pfx_pad_prefix` shapes, the degenerate-key branch for `ndx` *and* `pfx`, prefix-preservation properties, and round trips.\n* **`errno`**: `EINVAL` (22) verified for all 5 `*_from_string*` entry points × 8 out-of-range `hash_alg` values × 3 length shapes, with the output buffer untouched; `ctx_len > 0xff` confirmed *not* an error and to select a different DST path.\n\n## Rows I could not construct (documented in `documented_unreachable_error_rows`, with surrogate assertions)\n\nG6-002/013 (dead all-zero-`q` check), G6-024/034 (clamped `_is_inf`), G6-050/055/057/060/062 (`ge25519_is_on_curve` belt-and-braces), G6-066 (inner `_add` failure), G6-067 (`_string_to_points(n>2)` abort), G6-068 (elligator2 `fe25519_sqrt` abort), G6-096/097 (`assert(h_len <= 0xff)`), G6-104–109/119/120 (`mlen > SODIUM_SIZE_MAX` — not expressible in `unsigned long long`), G6-134 (`mlkem768_dec != 0`), G6-146 (`nonnull` NULL-pointer UB — deliberately not exercised).\n\n## Final `cargo test --no-default-features --no-fail-fast`\n\n```\ntests/t18_core_scalarmult_kem.rs  test result: ok. 37 passed; 0 failed  (4.16s)\ntests/t19_core_errors.rs         test result: ok. 27 passed; 0 failed  (1.90s)\n```\n\nEverything else in the suite also passes (t00–t12, t14–t17). One caveat outside my scope: `tests/t13_pwhash_errors.rs` (G2, another agent's file, appeared mid-run) fails/aborts in the same run — I did not touch it. Earlier in my session `t07_internal_lowlevel.rs` was failing on `_sodium_argon2_hash` / `_sodium_escrypt_r`; it is green now, so the G2 owner is actively fixing that area."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":338890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1673,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WrsYR539dBijXjs9pv3ndE","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"c06fc2e7-2952-4076-bf6c-f02f4ea7cf39","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:05.968Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B+C tests: core/scalarmult/kem/ipcrypt"}
