{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UghaTwo1t5oWYqas7i7am2","type":"tool_result","content":"[c] ss_push/max+1 -> (exit=0)\n[r] ss_push/max+1 -> (exit=0)\n[c] ss_pull/max+18 -> (exit=0)\n[r] ss_pull/max+18 -> (exit=0)\n[c] box_seal/max+1 -> (exit=0)\n[r] box_seal/max+1 -> (exit=0)\n[c] hmacsha256_init/segv/65 -> (exit=0)\n[r] hmacsha256_init/segv/65 -> (exit=0)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018AKqc9oZCiiirxxs7Qyssn","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"c83c5627-5bba-4b75-a481-5f6bf4f93b9c","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:44.698Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B+C tests: box/secretbox/sign/kx/auth"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mqiml3msrsbq3d42cvchadrjzgmg3dnfz63tovtszjjx6bxd74ua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Both deliverables are green.\n\n## Files\n\n| path | lines | `#[test]` fns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t10_sodium.rs` | 2994 | 28 |\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t11_sodium_errors.rs` | 2119 | 15 |\n\nEvery one of the 174 `CONFIGS.md ## G1` row ids is named in a t10 doc comment, and every one of the 159 `ERRORS.md ## G1` row ids is named in a t11 doc comment (verified programmatically).\n\n## Divergences found between C and Rust, and the fixes\n\n1. **`src/randombytes/os.rs` — missing live `assert(chunk_size > 0U)`** (ERRORS G1-140, the one *externally reachable* assert in this group). `randombytes_linux_getrandom()` in C does `if (size < chunk_size) { chunk_size = size; assert(chunk_size > 0U); }`. The Rust omitted the assert, so `randombytes_sysrandom_implementation.buf(p, 0)` — which bypasses `randombytes_buf`'s `size > 0` guard — returned quietly instead of raising SIGABRT (C: signal 6, Rust: exit 0). **Fix:** added the `chunk_size == 0 -> abort()` check.\n\n2. **`src/randombytes/mod.rs` — `.unwrap()` on the three *unchecked* implementation members** (ERRORS G1-133, G1-134, G1-135). The C performs **no** NULL check on `implementation_name`, `random` or `buf` (only `stir`/`uniform`/`close` are checked), so a custom impl leaving one NULL faults with **SIGSEGV**. The Rust used `Option::unwrap()`, which panicked and (with `panic = \"abort\"`) died with **SIGABRT** — wrong signal. **Fix:** added `call_name` / `call_random` / `call_buf` helpers that transmute the `Option<fn>` to a raw (possibly null) function pointer and call through it, reproducing the C exactly. Verified: C and Rust now both exit 139 (SIGSEGV) for all three rows.\n\n3. **Missing live `assert()`s (faithfulness fixes; none reachable from outside, all documented as such):**\n   - `src/randombytes/os.rs`: `assert(size <= 256U)` in `_randombytes_linux_getrandom`, and `assert(size > 0)` / `assert(size <= SSIZE_MAX)` in `safe_read` (rows G1-147, G1-148).\n   - `src/randombytes/internal.rs`: `assert(stream.nonce != 0)` (G1-150) and the two `assert(ret == 0)` on the chacha20 returns (G1-156, G1-157) — the return value was previously discarded.\n   - `src/sodium/codecs.rs`: `assert(b64_pos <= b64_len)` in `sodium_bin2base64` (G1-033).\n\nNothing else diverged: `bin2hex`/`hex2bin`/`bin2base64`/`base642bin`/`ip2bin`/`bin2ip`/`pad`/`unpad`/`memcmp`/`compare`/`is_zero`/`increment`/`add`/`sub`/`memzero`/`malloc`/`allocarray`/`free`/`mlock`/`mprotect_*`/`init`/`misuse`/`runtime_has_*`/`version_*` and all `randombytes_*` matched byte-for-byte, including `errno`, every out-parameter, `*hex_end`/`*b64_end` offsets and untouched buffer regions, under fuzzers of 4 000–20 000 randomised cases each.\n\n## Rows I could not construct (nearest reachable condition asserted instead)\n\n- **ERRORS G1-118** (`sodium_free` on a foreign pointer) — UB inside libc `free()`. Instead: a *scribbled* `sodium_malloc` region frees cleanly, proving no canary check exists.\n- **ERRORS G1-131 boundary** (`size == 0x4000000000` exactly, i.e. one below the guard) — would require a 256 GiB write. Only `size > 0x4000000000` is driven.\n- **ERRORS G1-141…G1-145, G1-147, G1-152, G1-153** (`/dev/urandom` fallback, `safe_read`, `poll` on `/dev/random`, device-open EIO) — unreachable on Linux x86-64 because the `getrandom(2)` probe succeeds. Proxy asserted out of process: with `sysrandom` installed, `randombytes_close()` returns `-1` before any stir and `0` *repeatedly* after, which is only possible on the getrandom path.\n- **ERRORS G1-090, G1-119, G1-120, G1-121, G1-122, G1-124, G1-125, G1-126, G1-127, G1-146, G1-154, G1-155, G1-158, G1-159, G1-033, G1-132** — dead code / unfireable in this build; each is recorded in `documented_unreachable_error_rows` with an observable proxy (plain-malloc pointer, no page protection, crit stubs always 0, `ULLONG_MAX == SIZE_MAX`, etc.).\n- **CONFIGS G1-047** as written in the table (`variant=7, b64=\"__\"`) is *not* a valid input — the C rejects it via the leftover-bits test at `codecs.c:319`. Both the rejection and the nearest valid input (`\"_w\"`) are asserted, with a comment.\n- **CONFIGS G1-173** (internal pool refill) can only be compared structurally (1000 draws, 1000 distinct, 8 refills) — the internal RNG is seeded from real entropy, so byte-level comparison is impossible.\n\n## Final `cargo test` summary\n\nAll 18 test binaries pass except `tests/t13_pwhash_errors.rs`, which is a **G2 (pwhash) file being written concurrently by another agent** — it aborts in `argon2_encode_string_rejections`. I confirmed it is not caused by my changes: the abort persists with my only `sodium/codecs.rs` edit disabled.\n\n```\nt00_harness      4 passed   t10_sodium         28 passed\nt01_constants    8 passed   t11_sodium_errors  15 passed\nt02_lowlevel    10 passed   t12_pwhash         26 passed\nt03_hashes      16 passed   t13_pwhash_errors  FAILED (other agent's G2 file, in flight)\nt04_aead        14 passed   t14_hash_errors    21 passed\nt05_aead_errors 12 passed   t15_hash_extra     15 passed\nt06_internal_exports 11 passed   t16_box_sign   29 passed\nt07_internal_lowlevel 22 passed  t17_box_sign_errors 21 passed\nlib unittests    5 passed   t18_core_scalarmult_kem 37 passed\n                            t19_core_errors    27 passed\n```\n\n`t10_sodium` and `t11_sodium_errors` were each run three times in default (parallel) mode with identical results — no intra-file races; all RNG-state-mutating rows run in child processes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":364220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":827,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Aw2j196PG6UFGUL4fdGJ7V","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"ba0a5fae-e606-4ad9-be2f-64f380a51467","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:10:46.576Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B+C tests: sodium+randombytes"}
