{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_s4gx4zai5wfgu6qzj3n5ioycnjxy2azsc5bsg2b2535jel457zpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: no `src/crypto_pwhash/**` file was touched — the Rust translation needed zero fixes.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n| file | lines | `#[test]`s |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t12_pwhash.rs` | 3068 | 29 |\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-rAO86K/translated_rust/tests/t13_pwhash_errors.rs` | 4055 | 30 |\n\nRow coverage is mechanically verified: every `G2-001…G2-148` (CONFIGS) id appears in a `t12` doc comment and every `G2-001…G2-223` (ERRORS) id appears in a `t13` doc comment, with no stray ids.\n\n## C/Rust divergences found: **none**\n\nZero fixes were needed under `src/crypto_pwhash/**`. The translation matched the C byte-for-byte on everything I could construct, including the non-obvious cases:\n\n* `strchr(itoa64, '\\0')` returning the *terminator*, so `escrypt_parse_setting` accepts a NUL as the `N_log2` character and decodes it as **64** (rather than failing) — exercised at all 14 setting positions × all 256 byte values.\n* The `size_t` wrap guards in `escrypt_kdf_nosse` (`need = B_size + V_size` and `need += XY_size`), reachable only at `N = 2^27, r = 1073741818` and `N = 2^28, r = 536870907`. Both wrap identically and yield `ENOMEM`.\n* `argon2_hash`'s `randombytes_buf(hash, hashlen)` pre-fill surviving a later failure, so `crypto_pwhash_argon2*` hands back *random* bytes (not zeros) with `-1` on an allocation failure. Identical bytes in both libraries.\n* `errno`-untouched vs `errno = EINVAL` distinctions (sentinel-based), e.g. `ARGON2_DECODING_FAIL` leaves `errno` alone while `ARGON2_VERIFY_MISMATCH` sets `EINVAL`.\n* Partial writes made *before* `sodium_misuse()` aborts (compared via `set_observation`).\n\n## ERRORS.md rows that are mis-stated (verified against the C)\n\n1. **G2-150 is wrong.** `sodium_bin2base64` does **not** return `NULL` when the destination is too small — libsodium 1.0.23 calls `sodium_misuse()` (`sodium/codecs.c:211-213`). So `argon2_encode_string`'s `SB(...) == NULL` branch is dead and the process **aborts (SIGABRT / exit 77)** instead. Exact boundaries (measured, C and Rust agree): for `Argon2_id` `dst_len 0..=27` and `50` → `ARGON2_ENCODING_FAIL`; `28..=49` and `51..=93` → `sodium_misuse()`; `>= 94` → OK. For `Argon2_i` every boundary shifts down by one (26 / 49 / 27..=48 / 50..=92 / 93). Moved to child-process rows (`encode/dst=…`, `encode_i/dst=…`, `hash_encoded/enc=…`).\n2. **G2-074's example is wrong** — `encodedlen = 40` for a 32-byte hash aborts rather than returning `ARGON2_ENCODING_FAIL`; only `0..=27` and `50` are `ENCODING_FAIL`. Also the minimum working `encodedlen` is **94**, not 72.\n3. **G2-205 is dead on 64-bit**, not constructible as the table suggests: after `r * p < 2^30` is enforced, `r > SIZE_MAX/128/p` implies `r * p > SIZE_MAX/128 >= 2^30` — a contradiction. Pinned by an assertion.\n4. **G2-136's examples** (`\"A\"`, `\"!!!\"`, empty hash field) give **two different** codes: `sodium_base642bin` only fails on a dangling 6-bit group, so `\"!!!\"`/`\"\"`/`\"YWJj~\"` decode to 0–3 bytes and are rejected by `argon2_validate_inputs` as `ARGON2_OUTPUT_TOO_SHORT (-2)`, while `\"A\"` and a trailing `'='` give `ARGON2_DECODING_FAIL (-32)`.\n\n## Rows downscaled or not constructible (all documented in-file)\n\n* **Downscaled:** CONFIGS G2-029/030/031/032 (argon2 MODERATE/SENSITIVE presets) and G2-088 (scrypt SENSITIVE, `N = 2^20`, ~1 GiB, ~8 s/lib) — only the constant accessors are compared; the same code paths are covered at cheap parameters. INTERACTIVE presets (G2-004, G2-015, G2-026, G2-084, G2-104) run exactly once each. CONFIGS G2-024 (`opslimit = OPSLIMIT_MAX`) cannot be hashed with, so acceptance is proved by classification (`EINVAL` from the `alg` switch vs `EFBIG` from the range check).\n* **Not constructible:** ERRORS G2-015/038/157 (`outlen > BYTES_MAX` — the unconditional leading `memset(out, 0, outlen)` precedes the check, so a real 4 GiB/128 GiB buffer would be needed; the *ordering* is pinned by a test), G2-037 (non-NUL-terminated `str` is UB via unbounded `strlen`), G2-072 (`malloc(hashlen)` failure needs allocator injection), G2-077/078/079 (`argon2_verify` mallocs are ≤128 bytes), G2-112/114, G2-219/220 (static, non-exported NULL guards).\n* **Dead (pinned by assertions where possible):** G2-010, G2-022/033/055/089/090/095/098 (unsigned `< 0`), G2-087/093/096/099/103/106/124/127/130/134 (`> UINT32_MAX` on `uint32_t`), G2-113 overflow half, G2-115 wrap half, G2-154/155, G2-156, G2-159/163/171/215 (`pickparams` always returns 0 — pinned by a 2000-sample replication plus a 200-sample sweep), G2-162, G2-164 (`pickparams` can never make `escrypt_gensalt_r` fail — pinned), G2-165/168/195, G2-183, G2-185/190/191/192/193/194 (\"can't happen\"), G2-196/209/213/222 (`munmap`, compiled out), G2-216 (pinned by exhaustively showing `validate_inputs` rejects every `m_cost < 8*lanes`), G2-223.\n\n## Final `cargo test --no-default-features`\n\n```\nt12_pwhash        : ok. 29 passed; 0 failed;  finished in 6.54s\nt13_pwhash_errors : ok. 30 passed; 0 failed;  finished in 0.14s\n```\nWhole suite green, warning-free: lib 5, t00 4, t01 8, t02 10, t03 16, t04 14, t05 12, t06 11, t07 22, t10 28, t11 15, **t12 29**, **t13 30**, t14 21, t15 15, t16 29, t17 21, t18 37, t19 27 — 0 failures anywhere.\n\nOne harness gotcha worth passing on to other groups: `reset_rngs()` mutates process-global state while `cargo test` runs a file's `#[test]`s in parallel threads, so any file with more than one RNG-dependent test needs its own mutex around each `reset_rngs; call C; reset_rngs; call Rust` sequence. Both of my files use a file-local `RNG_LOCK` for this (it caused a real, reproducible false failure before I added it)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":461095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":544,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UPVb62KCU2WLXnLML5Z8s2","session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"62d6d771-85fc-4fe8-859b-21733f74f7bf","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:35:30.838Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B+C tests: crypto_pwhash"}
