ODING_FAIL`, and the minimum working `encodedlen` is **94**, not 72. |\"),\n# G2-205\n(\"| G2-205 | `escrypt_kdf_nosse` | `r > SIZE_MAX / 128 / p` (e.g. `r` = 2^40, `p` = 2^24 — also caught by the `r*p` test first, so needs `r*p < 2^30`: `r` = 2^29, `p` = 1 passes `r*p` and `128*r*p` = 2^36, so use `r` = 0x7FFFFFFF with `p` = 1) | `errno = ENOMEM`, returns `-1` |\",\n \"| G2-205 | `escrypt_kdf_nosse` | `r > SIZE_MAX / 128 / p` | **CORRECTED (verified against the C):** this branch is **DEAD on 64-bit**. The preceding `r * p < 2^30` check makes it unsatisfiable: `r > SIZE_MAX/128/p` implies `r * p > SIZE_MAX/128 = 2^57 >= 2^30`, contradicting `r * p < 2^30`. Pinned by an assertion rather than constructed. (Would be `errno = ENOMEM`, `-1`.) |\"),\n# G2-136\n(\"| G2-136 | `argon2_decode_string` | output base64 invalid / too long for `ctx->outlen` budget, e.g. hash field `\\\"A\\\"`, `\\\"!!!\\\"`, or an empty hash field | returns `ARGON2_DECODING_FAIL` (=-32) |\",\n \"| G2-136 | `argon2_decode_string` | output base64 invalid / too long for the `ctx->outlen` budget | **CORRECTED (verified against the C):** the listed examples split across TWO codes, because `sodium_base642bin` only fails on a dangling 6-bit group. Hash field `\\\"!!!\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"` and `\\\"YWJj~\\\"` decode to 0-3 bytes and are then rejected by `argon2_validate_inputs` as `ARGON2_OUTPUT_TOO_SHORT` (=-2); hash field `\\\"A\\\"` or a trailing `'='` gives `ARGON2_DECODING_FAIL` (=-32). Both codes are asserted. |\"),\n]\nfor old, new in subs:\n    assert old in s, old[:80]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(\"4 rows corrected\")\nPY\ngrep -c 'CORRECTED (verified against the C)' ERRORS.md CONFIGS.md","description":"Correct the four G2 rows"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":535710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":881,"ephemeral_1h_input_toke