{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01H98mjnVh6ZyHfcKCziWbhF","type":"tool_result","content":"=== test suite ===\n18\n36521\nzsh: command not found: bc\n\n=== artifacts ===\nSYMBOLS.md     1093 lines\nERRORS.md       916 lines\nCONFIGS.md     1022 lines\n\n=== tooling ===\nHARNESS.md configs_G1.md configs_G2.md configs_G3.md configs_G4.md configs_G5.md configs_G6.md coverage.py errors_G1.md errors_G2.md errors_G3.md errors_G4.md errors_G5.md errors_G6.md feature_matrix.sh rowmap_mine.py symbol_audit.py verify_all.sh \n\n=== src files fixed ===\nsrc/crypto_generichash/blake2b/generichash_blake2b.rs\nsrc/randombytes/internal.rs\nsrc/randombytes/mod.rs\nsrc/randombytes/os.rs\nsrc/sodium/codecs.rs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"5b293f06-4036-4cc8-a41c-dc133a64adb6","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:52:03.921Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== test suite ===\n18\n36521\nzsh: command not found: bc\n\n=== artifacts ===\nSYMBOLS.md     1093 lines\nERRORS.md       916 lines\nCONFIGS.md     1022 lines\n\n=== tooling ===\nHARNESS.md configs_G1.md configs_G2.md configs_G3.md configs_G4.md configs_G5.md configs_G6.md coverage.py errors_G1.md errors_G2.md errors_G3.md errors_G4.md errors_G5.md errors_G6.md feature_matrix.sh rowmap_mine.py symbol_audit.py verify_all.sh \n\n=== src files fixed ===\nsrc/crypto_generichash/blake2b/generichash_blake2b.rs\nsrc/randombytes/internal.rs\nsrc/randombytes/mod.rs\nsrc/randombytes/os.rs\nsrc/sodium/codecs.rs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mrswljyokq2qxrb2qkjj77kokhm3v6ekr3duzzy6yw6zxl45abeq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. **`ALL CHECKS PASSED`** — reproducible with `.phaseA/verify_all.sh`.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | **890 / 890**, diff empty both ways; 0 non-libc undefined |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes | **923 / 923** (100%) |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | **856 / 856** (100%) |\n| holds under every feature combination | **1 / 1** — `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]` and `src/` has 0 `cfg(feature=…)`, so the power set has exactly one element (verified by `.phaseA/feature_matrix.sh`) |\n\n350 tests across 19 binaries, green in both serial and parallel mode.\n\n## What the differential tests found and fixed (Rust only; `c_src/` untouched)\n\nThe C build defines **no `HAVE_*` and no `NDEBUG`**, so `assert()` is *live* — the Rust had assumed otherwise, which produced 4 of the 5 bugs:\n\n1. **`randombytes/mod.rs`** — used `Option::unwrap()` on the *unchecked* impl members (`implementation_name`/`random`/`buf`). C does no NULL check, so it faults: C = **SIGSEGV**, Rust = SIGABRT (panic). Now calls through a raw, possibly-null pointer. Verified: both exit 139.\n2. **`randombytes/os.rs`** — missing live `assert(chunk_size > 0)`. `randombytes_sysrandom_implementation.buf(p, 0)` bypasses the `size > 0` guard: C = **SIGABRT**, Rust = returned quietly. Verified: both exit 134.\n3. **`crypto_generichash/blake2b/generichash_blake2b.rs`** — `_final` was missing `assert(outlen <= UINT8_MAX)`; Rust truncated `outlen as u8` and reached `sodium_misuse()` instead of a raw `abort()` — same signal, *different mechanism*, caught by the child-process comparison.\n4. **`randombytes/internal.rs`**, **`sodium/codecs.rs`** — further missing live asserts.\n\n## Notable methodology points\n\n- **Abort paths are compared, not skipped.** `sodium_misuse()` runs the installed handler before `abort()`, so the harness installs a handler that dumps the observable state and `exit(77)`. Child processes are then compared on exit code + signal + pre-abort side effects — e.g. `argon2_encode_string`'s whole `dst_len` 0…100 sweep resolved to **130 abort / 59 clean-fail / 17 success**, identical in both libraries.\n- **The 121 `_`-prefixed internal exports are driven directly** (`_sodium_softaes_*`, `_sodium_ge25519_*`, `_sodium_argon2_*`, `_sodium_escrypt_*`, …), including the 9 data v-tables called through their function pointers. This confirmed `softaes.rs` translated the live bitsliced branch, not the compiled-out LUT branch.\n- **7 Phase-A table rows were themselves wrong**; since the C is ground truth I corrected the rows and marked each `**CORRECTED (verified against the C)**` rather than bending a test to match the doc.\n- I fixed a latent race in my own harness (process-global RNG state under parallel tests) by making it thread-local — this independently resolved flakiness two sub-agents reported.\n\nOne caveat worth stating: 12 groups of rows are genuinely **not constructible** (multi-GiB/256-GiB buffers, `nonnull` NULL-pointer UB, unsigned `< 0` comparisons, `> UINT32_MAX` on `u32` fields). Each is listed in a `documented_unreachable_*` test that asserts the *constant or ordering* making it unreachable, rather than being silently dropped."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1003,"cache_read_input_tokens":556020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d07924e0-d479-4dd8-8d3b-8728ce2d0a77","uuid":"fba3251f-aae4-48bd-bbeb-44a735074e13","timestamp":"2026-08-23T09:52:25.848Z"}
